hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6601","Narrated to us Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Shahidi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Khusayf, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Makkah in the Farewell Pilgrimage, he said to his companions: ""With what did you enter ihram?"" Some of them said: With Hajj, some said: With Umrah, and some said: With what you entered ihram with, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""Then release all, except one who drove the sacrificial animal; for had I faced of my affair what I now look back on, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal until I am with you lawful."" He said: And he drove a hundred badanah to garland it. And Muhammad ibn Salamah did not mention the story of Suraqah."
"6602","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Musa ibn A'yan, from Khusayf, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: When I arrived with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his Hajj, he asked the people: ""With what did you enter ihram?"" People said: We entered ihram with Hajj, and others said: We arrived as mutamatti'un, and others said: We entered ihram with your ihram, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever arrived and did not drive a sacrificial animal, let him release; for had I faced of my affair what I now look back on, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal until I am lawful."" Then Suraqah ibn Malik said to him: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), is this Umrah of ours for our year, or forever? He said: ""No, rather forever."""
"6603","Narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Hushaym, from al-Hajjaj, from Ata, from Jabir, that Suraqah ibn Malik said: O Messenger of Allah, is this Umrah of ours for us specifically, or forever? He said: ""No, rather forever."""
"6604","Narrated to us Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti, narrated to us Wahb ibn Baqiyyah, informed us Khalid, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: We arrived with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanting only Hajj. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded whoever had no sacrificial animal with him to make it an Umrah. That was hard upon the people. Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah had a sacrificial animal with him, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, arrived from Yemen. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him: ""With what did you enter ihram?"" He said: With what you entered ihram with. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a sacrificial animal and a hundred sacrificial animals with him. Then Suraqah said: O Messenger of Allah, is this Hajj of ours for our year or forever? He said: ""No, rather forever."""
"6605","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, narrated to us Kathir ibn Yahya Abu Malik, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi, narrated to us Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with five remaining of Dhu al-Qa'dah, and entered Makkah with four passed of Dhu al-Hijjah. Then Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum said: O Messenger of Allah, is this tamattu' for us specifically or forever? He said: ""No, rather forever; Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."""
"6606","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mundhir al-Tariqi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fudayl, narrated to us Isma'il ibn Muslim, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We entered ihram with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and arrived in Makkah with four passed of Dhu al-Hijjah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to release it and make it an Umrah. So we released the full release; we circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, until when it was the day of Tarwiyah he commanded us, so we entered ihram for Hajj. Then some of us said to others: We left our land, until when only four remain between us and Mina, we go out with our male organs dripping semen? That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: ""Do you suspect me, while I am the trustee of the people of heaven and the people of earth? Indeed, had I faced of my affair what I now look back on, the sacrificial animal would only have been from Makkah."" And he did not mention the story of Suraqah."
"6607","Narrated to us Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti, narrated to us Safwan ibn Salih, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Muslim, narrated to us al-Awza'i, from Ata, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"6608","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Khatib al-Ahwazi, narrated to us Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali, narrated to us Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid, narrated to us Rabah ibn Abi Ma'ruf, from Ata, from Jabir, that Suraqah ibn Malik said: O Messenger of Allah, is the Umrah for this year of ours or forever? He said: ""No, rather forever."""
"6609","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, (ha) and narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Ali ibn Bahr and Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, they said: narrated to us Hatim ibn Isma'il, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, he said: Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum stood and said: Is our Umrah for this year of ours, or forever and ever? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interlaced his fingers one in the other and said: ""Umrah has entered into Hajj twice; no, rather forever and ever."""
"6610","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Suraqah ibn Malik. Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Suraqah ibn Malik, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his illness and said: Tell me about a stray that comes to the trough of my camels: is there reward for me if I give it water? He said: ""Yes, in the moist liver there is reward."""
"6611","Mujahid from Suraqah ibn Malik. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yunus, narrated to us Ata ibn Muslim, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Suraqah ibn Malik, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, do we act upon what the pen has dried upon and the decrees have run with, or for a future matter? He said: ""O Suraqah, act for what the pen has dried upon and the decrees have run with, for each is made easy."""
"6612","Ulayy ibn Rabah from Suraqah ibn Malik. Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Salih, narrated to us Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah, from his father, from Suraqah ibn Ju'shum, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Suraqah, shall I inform you of the people of Paradise and the people of Hell?"" He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""As for the people of Hell, every coarse, swaggering, arrogant one; and as for the people of Paradise, the weak, the overpowered."""
"6613","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati and Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti, they both said: narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi, narrated to us Wahb ibn Jarir, narrated to us Musa ibn Ulayy, from his father, from Suraqah ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Had I commanded anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband."""
"6614","Narrated to us Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Awfi, narrated to us Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah, (ha) and narrated to us Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Adam ibn Abi Iyas al-Asqalani, narrated to us al-Layth ibn Sa'd, from Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah, (ha) and narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Ibn al-Mubarak, from Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah, he said: I heard my father mentioning, from Suraqah ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Shall I guide you to the best charity: your daughter returned to you, having no earner besides you."""
"6615","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Mab Bahram al-Idhaji, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Marzuq, narrated to us Shahin ibn Hayyan, brother of Fahd, narrated to us Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah, he said: I heard my father narrating, from Suraqah ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Shall I inform you of the greatest charity: indeed of the greatest charity in reward is your daughter returned to you, having no earner besides you."""
"6616","Tawus from Suraqah ibn Malik. Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, informed me Qays ibn Sa'd, from Tawus, from Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum al-Mudliji, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, do we act something already concluded, or do we begin action anew? He said: ""Rather for an act already concluded."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, then for what is action? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Each is made easy for his deed."" He said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), now earnestness, now earnestness."
"6617","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf al-Uqayli, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Hatim ibn Ubayd Allah al-Namari, narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Abd al-Karim al-Dall, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Tawus, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he performed Hajj, Suraqah ibn Malik stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, deal with us the dealing of a people as if born today. When they came to the House he commanded them, so they circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then he stood at the top of the valley and addressed them, saying: ""Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."""
"6618","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Waki', (ha) and narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Yusuf, they both said: narrated to us Mis'ar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."""
"6619","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Raziyan, they both said: narrated to us Sahl ibn Uthman, narrated to us Ibn Abi Utbah, from Idris al-Awdi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah al-Zarrad, from Ata, from Tawus, from Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at al-Batha and said: ""Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."""
"6620","Al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah from Suraqah. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Amr al-Ash'athi, narrated to us Yunus ibn Bukayr, narrated to us Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, from Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together, and I heard him saying: ""Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."""
"6621","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum from his uncle Suraqah. Narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum, from his uncle Suraqah ibn Malik, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his illness in which Allah took him, and asked him; I asked him nothing but he informed me of it, until I remember something tonight of what I remember. He said: Of what I asked him was that I said to him: Tell me about a man who pours into his trough, and neglected camels and strays come to it: does he have reward in giving them water? He said: ""For you, in every moist liver there is reward."""
"6622","Narrated to us Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti, narrated to us Wahb ibn Baqiyyah, narrated to us Khalid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Malik, from Suraqah ibn Malik his uncle, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his illness in which Allah took him, and he mentioned like it."
"6623","Ka'b ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum from his brother Suraqah. Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Hassan ibn Ghalib, narrated to us Ibn Lahi'ah, narrated to me Yunus ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Abd Allah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father Ka'b ibn Malik, from Suraqah ibn Malik, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a stray that comes to his trough: does he have reward in it if he satiates it? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes, in every moist-livered creature there is reward."""
"6624","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, informed me Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b al-Mudliji, that his father informed him, that he heard Suraqah saying: Messengers of the disbelievers of Quraysh came to us, offering for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr the blood-money of each of them for whoever kills them or captures them. He said: While I was sitting in an assembly of my people's assemblies of Banu Mudlij, a man of them came until he stood over us and said: O Suraqah, I just now saw black shapes by the coast; I think it is Muhammad and his companions. Suraqah said: I knew it was them, so I said: They are not them, but you saw so-and-so and so-and-so who set out seeking. He said: I remained in the assembly only an hour, until I stood, entered my house, ordered my slave-girl to bring out my horse for me, she keeping it for me behind a hillock, and took my spear. I went out with it from the back of the house, drew with my spear in the ground, and lowered the spearhead, until I came to my horse and mounted it, and made it gallop, drawing near with me, until I saw their black shapes. When I drew near them where they could hear sound, my horse stumbled with me, so I fell from it. I stood, reached with my hand to my quiver, took out the divining arrows, and cast lots with them: shall I harm them or not? The one I disliked came out: that I not harm them. So I mounted my horse, disobeying the arrows, and made it gallop, drawing near with me to them again, until when I drew near I heard the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he not turning, while Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, looked around much. My horse's forelegs sank into the ground until they reached the knees, so I fell from it. I urged it, so it rose, its forelegs hardly coming out. When it stood upright, at the trace of its forelegs there was dust rising in the sky like smoke without fire. Ma'mar said: I said to Abu Amr ibn al-Ala: What is uthan? He was silent a while, then said: It is smoke without fire. Ma'mar said: Al-Zuhri said in his hadith: So I cast lots with the arrows, and the one I disliked came out: that I not harm them both. So I called to them with safety, and they stopped, and I mounted my horse until I came to them. And it had occurred to me, when I met from them what I met of being withheld from them, that the affair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will prevail. So I said to him: Your people have offered the blood-money for you. And I informed them of news of their journey and what people intend by them. And I offered them provisions and goods, but they took nothing from me, and asked me only: ""Conceal from us."" So I asked him to write for me a document of truce, by which I am secure. So he commanded Amir ibn Fuhayrah, and he wrote it for me on a piece of leather. Then he went on."
"6625","Narrated to us Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar al-Makki, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn Uqbah, narrated to me Ibn Shihab, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum al-Mudliji, that his father Malik informed him, that his brother Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum informed him, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out from Makkah emigrating to Madinah, Quraysh offered whoever returns him to them a hundred she-camels. He said: While I was sitting in my people's assembly, a man of us came and said: By Allah, I just now saw three riders pass by me; I think it is Muhammad. He said: So I gestured to him: Be silent, and said: They are but Banu so-and-so following a stray of theirs. He said: Perhaps. Then he was silent. I stayed a little, stood, ordered my horse, and it was led to the belly of the valley. I took my weapon from behind my chamber, then took my arrows with which I cast lots, then wore my armour. Then I took out my arrows and cast lots with them, and the one I disliked came out: he is not harmed. I hoped to return him, to take the hundred she-camels. So I mounted pursuing them. While my horse galloped with me it stumbled, so I fell from it. I took out my arrows and cast lots, and the arrow I disliked came out: he is not harmed. But I refused except to follow him, so I mounted it. When the people appeared to me and I looked at them, my horse stumbled with me, its forelegs going into the ground, so I fell. It extracted its foreleg, followed by smoke like uthan. So I knew he was protected from me, and that he is prevailing. So I called to them, saying: Wait for me; by Allah, I shall not harm you, nor shall anything you dislike come to you from me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Say to him: What does he seek?"" I said: Write for me a document between me and you as a sign. He said: ""Write, O Abu Bakr."" He said: So he wrote for me, then cast it to me. So I returned, kept silent, and mentioned nothing of what happened, until when Allah opened Makkah for His Messenger and he finished with the people of Hunayn, I went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the document he wrote for me. He said: While I headed to him, I entered among a squadron of the squadrons of the Ansar, and they began striking me with spears, saying: Away, away, until when I drew near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his she-camel, looking at his shins in his stirrup as if they were jumjarah, I raised my hand with the document and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is your document. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A day of fulfilment and piety, draw near."" So I accepted Islam. Then I remembered something to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about, and I recalled nothing but that I said: O Messenger of Allah, a stray comes to our troughs which I filled for my camels: is there reward for me in giving it water? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes, in every moist-livered creature there is reward."" So I departed, and drove to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) my charity."
"6626","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd, narrated to us my uncle, narrated to us my father, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, narrated to me Abd al-Rahman ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum al-Mudliji, that his father informed him, that Suraqah ibn Malik informed him, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out from Makkah emigrating to Madinah, Quraysh offered a hundred she-camels for whoever returns him. While I was sitting in my people's assembly, a man came and said: By Allah, I just now saw three riders pass by me; I think it is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I gestured to him: Be silent; they are but Banu so-and-so seeking a stray of theirs. I stayed a little, then stood, entered, ordered my horse, and it was led to the belly of the valley. I took my weapon from behind my chamber, then took my arrows with which I cast lots, and wore my armour. Then I took out my arrows and cast lots, and the arrow I disliked came out: that I not harm him. He said: I hoped to return him, to take the hundred she-camels. So I mounted pursuing him. While my horse galloped with me it stumbled, so I fell from it. I took out my arrows and cast lots with them, and the arrow I disliked came out: I shall not harm him. But I refused except to follow him, so I mounted my horse. When the people appeared to me and I looked at them, my horse stumbled with me, its forelegs going into the ground, and I fell from it. It extracted its forelegs, followed by smoke like a staff. So I knew that I was prevented from him, and that he is prevailing. So I called to them, saying: Wait for me; by Allah, I shall not harm you, nor shall anything you dislike come to you from me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What do you seek?"" I said: Write for me a document to be between me and you as a sign. He said: ""Write for him, O Abu Bakr."" He said: So he wrote a document for me, then cast them to me. He said: So I returned and kept silent, mentioning nothing of what happened, until when Allah, mighty and majestic, opened Makkah for His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he finished with Hunayn, I went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to meet him, with the document he wrote for me. While I headed to him I entered among a squadron of the squadrons of the Ansar, and they began striking me with spears, saying: Away, away, until I drew near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he being on his she-camel, looking at his shin in his stirrup as if it were jumjarah. So I raised my hand with the document and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is your document. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A day of fulfilment and piety."" So I accepted Islam, and drove to him the charity of my wealth."
"6627","Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Suraqah ibn Malik. Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tamattu', and we performed tamattu' with him. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for us, or is it forever? He said: ""Forever."""
"6628","An unnamed man from Suraqah ibn Malik. Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, narrated to us Zam'ah ibn Salih, from Muhammad ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, claiming that a man narrated to him of Banu Mudlij, he said: I heard my father saying: Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum came from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us such-and-such. Then a man said as if mocking: Did he not teach you how you defecate? He said: ""Yes; by Him who sent him with truth, he commanded us to lean upon the left, and to erect the right."""
"6629","660 - Suraqah ibn Amr ibn Atiyyah ibn Khansa al-Ansari, martyred on the day of Mu'tah. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahi'ah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah: ""Concerning the naming of those martyred on the day of Mu'tah of the Muslims, then of the Ansar, then of Banu al-Najjar, then of Banu Mazin ibn al-Najjar: Suraqah ibn Amr ibn Atiyyah ibn Khansa."""
"6630","661 - Suraqah ibn al-Hubab al-Ansari. Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Ibn Lahi'ah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah: Concerning the naming of those martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), of the Ansar, of Banu Amr ibn Awf, then of Banu al-Ajlan: Suraqah ibn al-Hubab."
"6631","Narrated to us Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani, narrated to us Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Concerning the naming of those martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), of the Ansar: Suraqah ibn al-Hubab ibn Adi ibn al-Ajlan."
"6632","Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: Concerning the naming of those martyred with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Khaybar, of the Ansar, then of Banu al-Ajlan: Murrah ibn Suraqah ibn Hubab. Thus said Ibn Shihab."
"6633","Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Harb, narrated to us Jarir ibn Hazim, from al-A'mash, from Sallam Abu Shurahbil, from Habbah and Sawa, the two sons of Khalid, they both said: We entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he treated something, and it tired him. He said: ""Do not despair of provision, as long as your heads move, for man is born by his mother red, with no skin upon him, then Allah provides for him."""
"6634","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Abu Mu'awiyah, from al-A'mash, from Sallam ibn Shurahbil, from Habbah and Sawa, the two sons of Khalid, they both said: We entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned like it."
"6635","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, narrated to us my father, narrated to us Waki' and Abu Mu'awiyah, from al-A'mash, from Sallam Abu Shurahbil, from Sawa ibn Khalid, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned like it."
"6636","Those named Sakhbarah. 663 - Sakhbarah al-Azdi. Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Ali ibn Bahr, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Razi, from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, from Abu Dawud, from Sakhbarah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is given and thanks, is tried and endures, wrongs then seeks forgiveness, and is wronged then forgives."" Then he was silent, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, what is for him? He said: ""Those, for them is security, and they are guided."""
"6637","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi, narrated to us Rubayh Abu Ghassan, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Mu'alla, from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, from Abu Dawud, from Abd Allah ibn Sakhbarah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like it."
"6638","Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Ali ibn Bahr, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Mu'alla, from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, from Abu Dawud, from Sakhbarah, he said: Two men passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he sat reminding, and he said: ""Sit, for you are upon good."" When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and his companions dispersed from him, they both stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, you said to us: ""Sit, for you are upon good."" Is it for us specifically, or for people generally? He said: ""There is no servant who seeks knowledge but it is expiation for what preceded."""
"6639","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi, narrated to us Rubayh Abu Ghassan al-Razi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Mu'alla, from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, from Abu Dawud, from Abd Allah ibn Sakhbarah, from Sakhbarah, he said: I sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he reminded, and two men passed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: ""Sit,"" and he mentioned similar to it."
"6640","Those named al-Sa'ib. 664 - Al-Sa'ib ibn Abi al-Sa'ib al-Makhzumi, and the name of Abu al-Sa'ib is Numaylah. Of his reports. Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Alluyah al-Qattan, narrated to us Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttali, narrated to us Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, narrated to me my master, he said: My family sent with me a bowl of milk and butter to their gods. So I went with it, and I feared to eat anything of it, so I put it down, when a dog came, drank the milk, ate the butter, and urinated upon the idol."
"6641","What al-Sa'ib narrated. Narrated to us Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi, narrated to us Sahl ibn Bakkar, narrated to us Wuhayb, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Mujahid, from al-Sa'ib ibn Abi al-Sa'ib, that he used to share with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in trade before Islam. When it was the day of the Conquest he came to him, and he said: ""Welcome to my brother and my partner: he neither evades nor disputes. O Sa'ib, you used to do deeds in Jahiliyyah not accepted from you, while today they are accepted from you."" And he was of precedence and kinship."
"6642","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, (ha) and narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, they both said: narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, narrated to us Sufyan, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from the guide of al-Sa'ib, from al-Sa'ib, that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""You were my partner in Jahiliyyah, and you were the best partner: you neither evade nor dispute."""
"6643","Narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sufyan ibn Sa'id al-Thawri, narrated to me Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Mujahid, from the guide of al-Sa'ib, from al-Sa'ib, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they began praising me and mentioning me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I know him best of you."" He said: You spoke truth, may my father and mother be ransom for you; you were my partner, and what an excellent partner you were: you neither evade nor dispute."
"6644","Narrated to us Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri, narrated to us Yusuf ibn Adi, (ha) and narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, they both said: narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, the freed slave of al-Sa'ib, from al-Sa'ib, that he used to say: Drink from the watering place of al-Abbas, for it is of the Sunnah."
"6645","665 - Al-Sa'ib ibn Khabbab, freed slave of Fatimah bint al-Walid ibn Utbah ibn Rabi'ah ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf. Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me al-Haytham ibn Kharijah, (ha) and narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani and Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, they said: narrated to us Isma'il ibn Ayyash, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayd Allah, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, he said: I saw al-Sa'ib ibn Khabbab smelling his garment, so I said to him: What is that, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""No ablution except from wind or sound."""
"6646","666 - Al-Sa'ib ibn Khallad al-Juhani. Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, they said: narrated to us Hudbah ibn Khalid, narrated to us Hammad ibn al-Ja'd, narrated to us Qatadah, narrated to me my father Khallad al-Juhani, from his father al-Sa'ib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you enters the privy, let him wipe with three stones."""
"6647","Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Missisi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan al-Ruhawi, narrated to us my father, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibn Khallad, from his father, like it."
"6648","667 - Al-Sa'ib ibn Khallad ibn Suwayd ibn Tha'labah al-Ansari. Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to us Ibn Lahi'ah, he said: I heard Hafs ibn Hashim ibn Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas mentioning that Khallad ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to him, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he supplicated, raised his palms to his face."
"6649","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, and narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, they both said: narrated to us al-Qa'nabi, from Malik, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Khallad ibn al-Sa'ib al-Ansari, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and commanded me to command my companions, or those with me, to raise their voices with talbiyah, or with ihlal. And he said: It is of the rites of Hajj."""
"6650","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Khallad ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father al-Sa'ib ibn Khallad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Command your companions to raise their voices with ihlal, for it is of the rites of Hajj."" Sufyan said: Ibn Jurayj had concealed a hadith from me; when Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr arrived to us I did not inform him. When he went out to Madinah I narrated it to him, and he said to me: O one-eyed, you hide narrations from us; when their people depart you inform us of them. I shall not narrate it from you. So he wrote to Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, and Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr wrote it to him. And Ibn Jurayj used to narrate it in his books: Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr wrote to me."
"6651","Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, from Khallad ibn al-Sa'ib ibn Suwayd al-Ansari, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Command your companions to raise their voices with ihlal, or he said: with talbiyah."""
"6652","Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Salim, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm wrote to me saying: Narrated to me Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, that Khallad ibn al-Sa'ib ibn Khallad ibn Suwayd al-Ansari narrated to him, from his father al-Sa'ib ibn Khallad, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Command your companions to raise their voices with talbiyah or ihlal; I do not know which of us erred, I or Abd al-Malik, in ihlal and talbiyah."""
"6653","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Humayd, narrated to us Hatim ibn Isma'il, from Rabi'ah ibn Uthman, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Khallad ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like it."
"6654","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, they both said: narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Khallad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever frightens the people of Madinah, Allah frightens him, and upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither sarf nor adl is accepted from him."""
"6655","Narrated to us Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim, narrated to me Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had, from Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir, from Ata ibn Yasar, from al-Sa'ib ibn Khallad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever frightens the people of Madinah, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."""
"6656","Narrated to us Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Ibn Abi Hazim, narrated to me Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from al-Sa'ib ibn Khallad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like it."
"6657","Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq, narrated to us Isma'il ibn Ja'far, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from al-Sa'ib ibn Khallad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like it."
"6658","Narrated to us Khalaf ibn Amr, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad, narrated to me Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from al-Sa'ib ibn Khallad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like it."
"6659","Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, they both said: narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri, narrated to us A'ishah bint al-Mundhir, she said: narrated to us Hisham ibn Urwah, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from al-Sa'ib ibn Khallad, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""O Allah, whoever wrongs the people of Madinah and frightens them, frighten him, and upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; Allah accepts from him neither sarf nor adl."""
"6660","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, (ha) and narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, they both said: narrated to us Zayd ibn al-Hubab, narrated to us Musa ibn Ubaydah, narrated to me Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Khalid ibn Khallad ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever frightens the people of Madinah, Allah, mighty and majestic, frightens him on the Day of Resurrection, curses him, is angry with him, and accepts from him neither sarf nor adl."""
"6661","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Humayd, narrated to us Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Labid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Ibrahim ibn Khallad ibn Suwayd, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, came and said: O Muhammad, be loud in crying labbayk and abundant in shedding blood, meaning by ajj: talbiyah, and by thajj: blood."""
"6662","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Humayd, narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Musa al-Taymi, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from al-Sa'ib ibn Suwayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is nothing that befalls the crop of one of you from the wild foragers but Allah writes for him reward by it."""
"6663","668 - Al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid al-Kindi, son of the sister of al-Namir ibn Qasit. Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr, he said: ""Al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid died in the year ninety-one, and it is said: he died in the year eighty-two."""
"6664","What al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid narrated. Yazid ibn al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid from his father. Narrated to us Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali, narrated to us Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from his grandfather, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Let none of you take the goods of his companion, in jest or in earnest; and when one of you takes the staff of his companion, let him return it to him."""
"6665","Al-Zuhri from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid. Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Dhahabi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had but one mu'adhdhin; none other called adhan for him. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon the pulpit on Friday, he called adhan at the door of the mosque; when he descended, he established the prayer. Then Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, was likewise; then Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, was likewise; until when it was Uthman, people multiplied, so he commanded the first call in the market at a house of his called al-Zawra. So adhan was called for him upon it; when Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, sat upon the pulpit, his first mu'adhdhin called adhan; when he descended, he established the prayer."
"6666","Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, (ha) and narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Abu Umar al-Darir, they both said: narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he had a mu'adhdhin; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon the pulpit, he called adhan; when he descended, he established. That was in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the time of Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. When it was Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, people spread and multiplied, so he commanded a mu'adhdhin, and he called adhan at al-Zawra before his coming out, informing the people that Friday had arrived."
"6667","Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth, narrated to us al-Ashja'i, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: The first adhan on Friday in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon the pulpit, he called adhan; when he descended, he established. That was in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the time of Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. When it was Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, people spread and multiplied, so he commanded a mu'adhdhin, and he called adhan at al-Zawra before his coming out."
"6668","Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Ibn Idris, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, like it."
"6669","Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la, (ha) and narrated to us Abdan, narrated to us Huraym ibn Abd al-A'la, they both said: narrated to us Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman, narrated to me my father, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: The call was in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, at the pulpit; and the first to introduce the last call was Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him."
"6670","Narrated to us Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali, narrated to us Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, nephew of al-Namir ibn Qasit: that the call on Friday, its first was when the imam sat, and when the prayer stood, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, until when it was Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, and people multiplied, he added the third call at al-Zawra."
"6671","6648 - Narrated to us Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Salih, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, informed me Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, informed me al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid: that the adhan, the first of it was when the imam sat on the minbar on Friday, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar; then when it was the caliphate of Uthman and the people increased, Uthman ibn Affan ordered on Friday the third adhan, so it was called on al-Zawra'."
"6672","6649 - Narrated to us Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Salih, narrated to us Anbasah ibn Khalid, narrated to us Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid. [Same report as above.]"
"6673","And narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Shihab, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: Uthman only ordered the third call to prayer on Friday when the people of Madinah increased; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had no more than one mu'adhdhin, and the adhan on Friday was only when the imam sat."
"6674","6650 - Narrated to us al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih, narrated to me al-Layth, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, narrated to me al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, that the calling of the adhan... and he mentioned the like of it."
"6675","6651 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri, narrated to us Yusuf ibn Adi, narrated to us Rushdin ibn Sa'd, from Qurrah and Uqayl and Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, he said: informed me al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid: that the adhan, the first of it was when the imam sat on the minbar on Friday in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them."
"6676","6652 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd, narrated to us my uncle, narrated to us my father, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, that al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, son of the sister of Namir, informed him that: Uthman ibn Affan only ordered the third call when the people of Madinah increased; he said: and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had no more than one mu'adhdhin, so the call on Friday was when the imam sat."
"6677","6653 - Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, (h) and narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us al-Qa'nabi and Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi, (h) and narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me my father, they said: narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: I was among the boys who went out to Thaniyyat al-Wada' to meet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk."
"6678","6654 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi, narrated to us Hibban ibn Musa and Suwayd ibn Nasr, they said: narrated to us Ibn al-Mubarak, from Yunus, (h) and narrated to us Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Salih, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, informed me Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, that al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid informed him, that Shurayh al-Hadrami was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: That is a man who does not take the Qur'an as a pillow."
"6679","6655 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, narrated to us Wahb ibn Jarir, narrated to us my father, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Rashid narrating from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had Makhramah ibn Shurayh al-Hadrami mentioned before him, so he said: That is a man who does not take the Qur'an as a pillow."
"6680","6656 - Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, narrated to us Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, (h) and narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Musaffa, narrated to us Baqiyyah, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: There was no public exhortation in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor Abu Bakr nor Umar, until the first who gave exhortations was Tamim al-Dari; he sought permission from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, so he permitted him, and he exhorted standing."
"6681","6657 - Narrated to us Abu Usamah al-Halabi, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani' al-Rusafi, narrated to us my grandfather, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion, no Safar, and no Hamah."
"6682","6658 - Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn al-Bakhtari al-Ta'i, narrated to us Bishr ibn Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah, from his father, (h) and narrated to us Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Hawti, narrated to us Abu al-Yaman, narrated to us Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion, no Safar, and no Ham."
"6683","6659 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i, informed Abu Umayyah Amr ibn Hisham, he said: I found in the book of Attab, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion, no Safar, and no Ham."
"6684","6660 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Salamah ibn Abi Kabshah, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the jizyah from the Magians of Hajar, and Umar ibn al-Khattab took it from the Magians of Persia, and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, took it from the Berbers."
"6685","6661 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Khayyat, he said: narrated to us Abu Khalid al-Ahmar, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver on Friday two sermons, sitting between them."
"6686","6662 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, narrated to us Hisham ibn Ammar, narrated to us al-Walid ibn Muslim, narrated to us Ibn Lahi'ah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, did not appoint a judge, and the first who appointed judges was Umar, may Allah be pleased with him; he said to him: Ward off the people from me in the dirham and the two dirhams."
"6687","6663 - Narrated to us Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madani, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, narrated to us Ma'n ibn Isa, from Isa ibn Sabrah Abu Ubadah al-Zuraqi, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: The seal of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the hand of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, until he died, then in the hand of Umar until he died, then in the hand of Uthman until it fell into the well of Aris."
"6688","6664 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakkar, narrated to us Abu Ma'shar, from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: The blood-money in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was one hundred camels of four age-classes: twenty-five hiqqah, twenty-five jadha'ah, twenty-five daughters of labun, and twenty-five daughters of makhad, until it was the time of Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he founded the garrison cities. Umar said: Not all people can find camels, so value the camels ounce by ounce; so it was four thousand dirhams. Then camels became dear, so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Value the camels; so the camels were valued at an ounce and a half, so it was six thousand dirhams. Then camels became dear, so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Value the camels; so they were valued at two ounces, so it was eight thousand dirhams. Then camels became dear, so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Value the camels; so they were valued at three ounces, so it was twelve thousand. So he set upon the people of silver twelve thousand, and upon the people of camels one hundred camels, and upon the people of gold one thousand dinars, and upon the people of garments two hundred garments, the value of each garment five dinars, and upon the people of sheep one thousand ewes, and upon the people of goats one thousand she-goats, and upon cattle two hundred cows."
"6689","6665 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari, narrated to us Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Sulaym, from Rushdin ibn Sa'd, from Yunus ibn Yazid and Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed the fay' which Allah granted at Hunayn from the spoils of Hawazin, and he spread the distribution among the people of Makkah from Quraysh and others, so the Ansar became angry. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that, he came to them in their dwellings, then said: Whoever is here and is not of the Ansar, let him go out to his lodging. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) testified and praised Allah, Mighty and Majestic, then said: O company of Ansar, there has reached me some of your talk about these spoils by which I favored men, conciliating them to Islam, that perhaps they will bear witness after this day, and Allah has brought Islam into their hearts. Then he said: O company of Ansar, did not Allah favor you with faith, and single you out with honor, and name you with the best of names: the helpers of Allah and the helpers of His Messenger? And were it not for the Hijrah I would have been a man of the Ansar; and if the people took a valley and you took a valley, I would take your valley. Will you not be pleased that the people go with these spoils, the sheep and cattle and camels, and you go with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? When the Ansar heard the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they said: We are pleased. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Answer me in what I said? So the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, you found us in darkness, so Allah brought us out by you to light; and you found us on the brink of a pit of Fire, so Allah saved us by you; and you found us astray, so Allah guided us by you. Then they affirmed, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for them."
"6690","Khusayfah Abu Yazid from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid. 6666 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Warraq al-Wasiti, narrated to us Khalid ibn Makhlad, narrated to me Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik al-Nawfali, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from his father, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met slave-girls singing, saying: You greet us, we greet you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped, then called them and said: Do not say thus, but say: May Allah greet us and you. So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, do you permit the people in this? He said: Yes, it is marriage, not fornication; proclaim the marriage."
"6691","6667 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyabi, narrated to us Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik, from his father, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from his father, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when his son Tahir died, the eye of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shed tears. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, did you weep? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The eye sheds, and tears overcome, and the heart grieves, and we do not disobey Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"6692","6668 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nasr al-Sa'igh, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyabi, narrated to us Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik, from his father, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, that his father informed him, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None shall enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a grain of pride. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are ruined; how are we to know what is in our hearts of that pride, and where is it? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears wool, or milks the sheep, or eats with what his right hand owns, then there is not in his heart, if Allah wills, pride."
"6693","Yazid ibn Khusayfah from al-Sa'ib. 6669 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore two coats of mail together on the day of Uhud."
"6694","6670 - Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, narrated to me Ibn Lahi'ah, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: It suffices a man in supplication to say: O Allah, forgive me and have mercy on me and admit me into Paradise."
"6695","6671 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Asbagh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, narrated to me Abdullah ibn al-Aswad al-Qurashi, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My community shall remain upon the fitrah as long as they pray Maghrib before the rising of the stars."
"6696","6672 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul, narrated to us Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks an intoxicant, whatever it be, Allah shall not accept from him prayer for forty days."
"6697","6673 - Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, narrated to me al-Layth, from Ibn al-Had, from Isma'il ibn Abdullah ibn Ja'far, he said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who is in a gathering, then says when he wants to rise: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You, except he is forgiven what was in that gathering. So I narrated this hadith to Yazid ibn Khusayfah, so he said: Thus narrated to me al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6698","6674 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Hisham ibn Ammar, narrated to us Yahya ibn Hamzah, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, that he informed him, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been favored over the prophets with five: I was sent to all mankind, and I stored my intercession for my community, and I was aided with awe for a month before me and a month behind me, and the earth was made for me a mosque and a purification, and spoils were made lawful for me and were not lawful for anyone before me."
"6699","6675 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, narrated to us Ali ibn Bahr, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb, informed me Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah, (h) and narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, narrated to us Hisham ibn Ammar, narrated to us Yahya ibn Hamzah, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: I complained of illness in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I was carried to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw him treating me with the Qur'an, and he blew upon me with it; and the wording is that of Hisham ibn Ammar."
"6700","Sa'd ibn Sa'id al-Ansari from al-Sa'ib. 6676 - Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani, narrated to us Isma'il ibn Abi Uways, narrated to me Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id, he said: I heard al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid al-Kindi, son of the sister of al-Namir, saying: Prayer was enjoined two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs; then it was increased in the prayer of residence, and the prayer of travel was left as it was."
"6701","6677 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us al-Qa'nabi, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: Prayer was enjoined two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs; then it was increased in the prayer of residence, and the prayer of travel was left as it was."
"6702","Muhammad ibn Yusuf from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid. 6678 - Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, (h) and narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, narrated to us Hatim ibn Isma'il, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: I was taken for Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and I was seven years old."
"6703","6679 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Nu'aym ibn Hammad, narrated to us Hatim ibn Isma'il, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"6704","6680 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki, narrated to us Bishr ibn Isa ibn Marhum al-Attar, narrated to us Hatim ibn Isma'il, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, or another - Bishr doubted - from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: My maternal aunt took me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my sister's son is ill. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, and I drank his ablution water; then I stood behind his back, and I saw his seal between his shoulders like the button of the bridal canopy."
"6705","Al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman from al-Sa'ib. 6681 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani, from al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid said to me: The sa' in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a mudd and a third of your mudd of today; then it was increased in the time of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. He said: And al-Sa'ib said: I was taken for Hajj in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was a boy."
"6706","6682 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Hisham ibn Ammar, (h) and narrated to us Musa ibn Harun and Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, they said: narrated to us Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, they said: narrated to us Hatim ibn Isma'il, from al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid saying: My maternal aunt took me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my sister's son is in pain. So he wiped my head and supplicated for me for blessing; then he performed ablution, and I drank from his ablution water; then I stood behind his back, and I looked at his seal between his shoulders like the button of the bridal canopy."
"6707","6683 - Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, narrated to us Hatim ibn Isma'il, from al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid saying: In the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and part of the time of Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, we did not flog for wine until they exceeded therein; so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, flogged eighty, but they were not deterred; so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, fixed therein eighty, and said: When he becomes drunk he slanders, and speaks falsehood."
"6708","6684 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani, narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Hurayth, narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Musa, from Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, informed me al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: A man was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they said: O Messenger of Allah, this man stole the covering of a camel or the covering of a beast. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not think he did it. Then they said: O Messenger of Allah, this man stole. He said: I do not think he did it, until he testified against himself several testimonies. So he said: Take him and cut him; then bring him to me. So they cut him, then they brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Woe to you, repent to Allah. He said: I repent to Allah. He said: O Allah, turn to him."
"6709","6685 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami' al-Basri, narrated to us Abdah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Marwazi, narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani, from al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I was with al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid when al-Zubayr ibn Suhayl ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came to him, and on his face was the mark of prostration. When he saw him he said: Who is this? It was said: Al-Zubayr. He said: This one has ruined his face. By Allah, it is not the mark which Allah named; and I have prayed upon my face for eighty years, and prostration has not left a mark between my eyes."
"6710","6686 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us Ali ibn Bahr, narrated to us Makki ibn Ibrahim, from al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, that a woman entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O A'ishah, do you know this one? She said: Yes, so she sang to her. So he said: Satan has blown into her nostrils."
"6711","Yusuf ibn Ya'qub from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid. 6687 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me Muhammad ibn Bakkar, narrated to us Abu Ma'shar, from Yusuf ibn Ya'qub, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bring out Abdullah ibn Hanzal from beneath the curtains of the Ka'bah, then he killed him, then said: No Qurashi shall be killed after this in captivity."
"6712","Abu Mawdud Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Sulayman al-Madani from al-Sa'ib. 6688 - Narrated to us Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, narrated to us Isa ibn al-Mughirah ibn al-Dahhak, narrated to me Abu Mawdud Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Sulayman, he said: I heard al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah from the expedition of Tabuk, the people went out to meet him; so the women and boys went out. Al-Sa'ib said: So I was among those who met him with the boys, until we met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Thaniyyat al-Wada'."
"6713","Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah al-Nawfali from al-Sa'ib. 6689 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari, narrated to us Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik al-Nawfali, from his father, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent suhur are dates. And he said: May Allah have mercy on those who take suhur."
"6714","6690 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari, narrated to us Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik, from his father, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent condiment is vinegar."
"6715","6691 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Khalid ibn Yazid, narrated to us Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik, from his father, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man behind him turning over pebbles while he was in prayer, so he said: Who was turning over the pebbles? A man said: I. So he said: That is your share of your prayer."
"6716","Dawud ibn Qays al-Farra' from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid. 6692 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad, they said: narrated to us Hisham ibn Ammar, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri, narrated to us Dawud ibn Qays al-Madani, he said: I heard al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought protection for me with the Opening of the Book, with spittle."
"6717","Ata', freedman of al-Sa'ib, from al-Sa'ib. 6693 - Narrated to us Sahl ibn Musa al-Ramahurmuzi, narrated to us al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari, narrated to us al-Nadr ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Ikrimah ibn Ammar, narrated to us Ata', freedman of al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, brother of al-Namir ibn Qasit, he said: The middle of al-Sa'ib's head was black, and the rest of his head and his beard white. So I said to him: O my master, by Allah, I have never seen a head like this of yours: this white and this black. He said: Shall I not tell you, O my son? I said: Yes. He said: I was with boys playing, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me; so I came before him and greeted him. So he said: And upon you; who are you? So I said: I am al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, brother of al-Namir ibn Qasit. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped my head and said: May Allah bless you. He said: So by Allah, it shall never turn white; or he said: It shall remain thus forever."
"6718","Al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid. 6694 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, narrated to us Yahya ibn Kathir al-Anbari, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Kathir, narrated to us al-Zubayr, meaning Ibn al-Khirrit, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed Hasan, so al-Aqra' ibn Habis said to him: Ten have been born to me, I have not kissed any of them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah shall not have mercy on him who does not have mercy on people."
"6719","Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydullah from al-Sa'ib. 6695 - Narrated to us Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar al-Makki, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi, narrated to me Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah, he said: I was with my uncle Isa ibn Talhah in the mosque, and al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid entered; so he sent me to him and said: Go to that shaykh and say to him: Your nephew Isa ibn Talhah says to you: Have you seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So I went to him, and he said: Yes, I have seen him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and I entered upon him, I and young boys with me, and we found him eating dates in a basket, and with him were men of his companions; so he took for us from those dates a handful, and wiped over our heads."
"6720","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz from al-Sa'ib. 6696 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Umar al-Allaf al-Razi, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra', from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of unlawful earning are: the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the earnings of a cupper."
"6721","Those named Sulayk. 669 - Sulayk ibn Amr, and it is said Ibn Hudbah al-Ghatafani. 6697 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar and al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: A man called Sulayk from Ghatafan came, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon standing, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Sulayk, stand and bow two light rak'ahs."
"6722","6698 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Ma'mar al-Qati'i and Dawud ibn Rushayd, they said: narrated to us Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, (h) and Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: Sulayk al-Ghatafani came, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Pray two rak'ahs and be brief in them."
"6723","6699 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far Ghundar, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from al-Walid Abu Bishr, from Talhah, meaning Ibn Nafi', that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah narrating that Sulayk came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, so he sat; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to pray two rak'ahs, being brief in them."
"6724","6700 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, informed me Amr ibn Dinar, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: A man came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the minbar on Friday delivering the sermon, so he said to him: Have you bowed two rak'ahs? He said: No. He said: Then bow."
"6725","6701 - Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us Shu'bah, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while delivering the sermon: When one of you comes on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon, or has already come out, let him pray two rak'ahs."
"6726","6702 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi, (h) and narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, they said: narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muslim, informed us Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon on Friday, and a man entered; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you prayed? He said: No. He said: Then pray. He said: So he bowed two rak'ahs."
"6727","6703 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith, narrated to us my father, from Habib, from Amr, from Jabir, that a man from Ghatafan came on Friday while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you prayed? He said: No. He said: Prostrate two prostrations, and be quick in them."
"6728","6704 - Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, he said: A man entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the minbar delivering the sermon on Friday, standing, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you prayed? He said: No. He said: Then pray two rak'ahs."
"6729","6705 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sawa', narrated to us Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, that a man entered while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to pray two rak'ahs."
"6730","6706 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Isma'il ibn Ulayyah, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, he said: A man came on Friday while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, so he said: Have you prayed? He said: No. He said: Stand and bow."
"6731","6707 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Arim Abu al-Nu'man, they said: narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: A man came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was addressing the people, so he said: Have you prayed, O so-and-so? He said: No. He said: Stand and bow."
"6732","6708 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Furat al-Qazzaz, narrated to us Hibban ibn Ali, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, so he ordered him to pray two rak'ahs."
"6733","6709 - Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, narrated to us Sufyan, narrated to us Abu al-Zubayr, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: Sulayk ibn Amr al-Ghatafani entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the minbar delivering the sermon on Friday, standing, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you prayed? He said: No. He said: Then pray two rak'ahs."
"6734","6710 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat al-Kufi, narrated to us Minjab ibn al-Harith, narrated to us Ali ibn Mushir, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Jabir, he said: Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon on the minbar on Friday; so he ordered him to pray two rak'ahs, being brief in them."
"6735","6711 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani, narrated to us Abu Umayyah, son-in-law of Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti, narrated to us Amr ibn Awn, narrated to us Hushaym, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from al-Hasan, from Jabir, he said: Sulayk al-Ghatafani came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to pray two rak'ahs, being brief in them, and said: When one of you comes while the imam is delivering the sermon, let him pray two rak'ahs, being brief in them."
"6736","6712 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Salamah ibn Abi Kabshah, narrated to us Safwan ibn Isa, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Sulayk al-Ghatafani, that he came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon on the minbar, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you bowed? He said: No. He said: Then pray two rak'ahs, being brief in them."
"6737","What Sulayk narrated. 6713 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ayyub al-Dabbi, from Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari, from Jabir, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Sulayk al-Ghatafani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Perform ablution from the meat of camels, and do not perform ablution from the meat of sheep; and pray in the resting places of sheep, and do not pray in the kneeling places of camels."
"6738","Abi al-Lahm, and his name. 6714 - Narrated to us al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Salih, narrated to me al-Layth, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Yazid ibn al-Had, that Umayr, freedman of Abi al-Lahm, informed him, from Abi al-Lahm, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the stones of oil, while he was covering himself with his hands, supplicating."
"6739","Those named Sidan. 671 - Sidan Abu Abdullah. 6715 - Narrated to us Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim Abu Ubaydah al-Askari, narrated to us Yunus ibn Musa al-Sami, narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Hammad, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn al-Ghasil, from Abdullah ibn Sidan, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked over the people of the well, and said: O people of the well, have you found what your Lord promised true? So they said: O Messenger of Allah, do they hear? He said: They hear as you hear, but they do not answer."
"6740","Those named Surraq. 672 - Surraq. 6716 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Mu'alla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili, (h) and narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, they said: narrated to us Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, he said: I was in Egypt, and a man said to me: Shall I not point you to a man of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes. So he pointed to a man beside him. So I said: Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I am Surraq. So I said: Glory be to Allah, you should not be named by this name while you are a man of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Surraq, so I shall never leave it. He said: I said: And why did he name you Surraq? He said: A man of the desert people came with two camels of his to sell them, so I bought them from him, and I said to him: Go along until I give you. So I entered my house and spent the price of the two camels on my need, and I hid until I thought the Bedouin had left. So I came out and there was the Bedouin waiting. So he seized me and brought me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and informed him of the news. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What carried you to what you did? I said: I spent their price on my need, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then pay him. I said: I have nothing. He said: You are Surraq; go with him, O Bedouin, and sell him until you take your right in full. So the people began to bargain for him, and he would turn to them and say: What do you want? They said: We want to ransom him from you. He said: So by Allah, none of you is more in need of Allah than I. Go, for I have freed you."
"6741","6717 - Narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Juwayriyah ibn Asma', from Abdullah ibn Yazid, freedman of al-Munba'ith, from men of the people of Egypt, from a man of them called Surraq: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with a witness and an oath."
"6742","Those named Sabit. 674 - Sabit Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi. 6718 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us Abu Burdah, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is afflicted with a calamity, let him remember his calamity by me, for it is the greatest of calamities to him."
"6743","Those named Sayyar. 675 - Sayyar ibn Bilzq Abu Abi al-Ushara' al-Darimi, and the name of al-Ushara' is Ballan. 6719 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Arim Abu al-Nu'man, (h) and narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, they said: narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Abi al-Ushara' al-Darimi, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is slaughtering only from the throat or the brisket? He said: If you stabbed it in its thigh, it would suffice you."
"6744","6720 - Narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Hasan ibn Bakr ibn al-Sharud al-San'ani, narrated to me my father, from my grandfather, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Abi al-Ushara' al-Darimi, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is slaughtering only in the throat or the brisket? He said: If you stabbed it in its thigh, it would suffice you."
"6745","6721 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani, narrated to us Abu Mahdhurah Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah, narrated to us Dawud ibn Shabib, narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Abi al-Ushara' al-Darimi, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is slaughtering only in the throat? He said: If you stabbed it in its thigh, it would suffice you."
"6746","6722 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammali al-Asbahani, narrated to us Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays al-Dabbi, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Abi al-Ushara' al-Darimi, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Atirah, so he deemed it good."
"6747","6723 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Shahriyar, narrated to us my father, (h) and narrated to us Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti, narrated to us Sa'd Abu al-Radi, they said: narrated to us Muhammad ibn Mus'ab al-Qarqasani, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Abi al-Ushara', from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while my father was dying, so he spat upon him from his horn to his foot; it is as if I see the specks of spittle upon his body."
"6748","Those named Siyabah. 676 - Siyabah ibn Asim al-Sulami. 6724 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti, narrated to us Hushaym, narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amr ibn Sa'id ibn al-As, informed me Siyabah ibn Asim al-Sulami, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Hunayn: I am the son of the Awatik."
"6749","677 - Simawayh. 6725 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani, narrated to us Salih ibn Qatan al-Bukhari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Miskin al-Azdi, narrated to us Mansur ibn Subayh, brother of al-Rabi' ibn Subayh, narrated to me Simawayh, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I heard from his mouth to my ear; and we carried wheat from al-Balqa' to Madinah, so we sold, and we wanted to buy the dates of Madinah, but they prevented us. So we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them, to those who prevented us: Does not the cheapness of this food suffice you despite the dearness of these dates which they carry? Leave them to carry it. And Simawayh was from al-Balqa', a Christian verger, then he embraced Islam and his Islam was good, and he lived one hundred and twenty years."
"6750","Those named Sandar. 678 - Sandar Abu Abdullah, freedman of Zinba' al-Judhami. 6726 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar, narrated to us Ibn Lahi'ah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Rabi'ah ibn Laqit al-Tujibi, from Abdullah ibn Sandar, from his father, that he was with al-Zinba' ibn Salamah al-Judhami, so he became angry with him and castrated him and cut his nose; and he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so he spoke harshly to al-Zinba', and freed him from him. He said: Advise concerning me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I advise with every Muslim."
"6751","Those named Sa'r. 679 - Sa'r al-Du'ali. 6727 - Narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abu Murarah al-Juhani, from Abu Sa'r al-Du'ali, from his father, he said: I was in the district of Makkah, and a Muslim man came while I was among my sheep. So I said: Who are you? So he said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah. So I said: Welcome to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah. What do you want? He said: I want the charity of your sheep. He said: So I brought him a ewe that had just given birth when it delivered. When he looked at it he said: Our right is not in this. I said: Then in what is your right? He said: In the thaniyyah and the fat jadha'ah."
"6752","Those named Samurah. 680 - Samurah ibn Mi'yar Abu Mahdhurah al-Jumahi, mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and he is Samurah ibn Mi'yar ibn Wahb ibn Du'mus ibn Sa'd ibn Jumah; and there is disagreement about his name. Ibn al-Kalbi said: His name is Aws ibn Mi'yar. 6728 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, (h) and narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz, narrated to us Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi, (h) and narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, (h) and narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar, narrated to us Affan, they said: narrated to us Hammam, narrated to us Amir al-Ahwal, narrated to me Makhul, that Ibn Muhayriz narrated to him, that Abu Mahdhurah narrated to him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him the adhan in nineteen phrases, and the iqamah in seventeen phrases. The adhan: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; [I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah]; hasten to prayer, hasten to prayer; hasten to success, hasten to success; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah. And the iqamah doubled, doubled."
"6753","6729 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Rahawayh, narrated to us Mu'adh ibn Hisham, from his father, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Makhul, from Abdullah ibn Muhayriz, from Abi Mahdhurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me the adhan, so he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; then he returns and says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; hasten to prayer, hasten to prayer; hasten to success, hasten to success; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah."
"6754","6730 - Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati, narrated to us Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti, narrated to us Abdah ibn Sulayman, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid, from Makhul, from Abdullah ibn Muhayriz, from Abi Mahdhurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me the adhan in nineteen phrases, and the iqamah in seventeen phrases."
"6755","6731 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa, narrated to us Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad, narrated to us Ibn Jurayj, narrated to me Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah, that Abdullah ibn Muhayriz narrated to him, and he was an orphan in the care of Abu Mahdhurah, so he equipped him to Sham. He said: So I said to Abu Mahdhurah: I am going out to Sham, and I fear I shall be asked about your adhan. So he informed me that Abu Mahdhurah informed him, he said: I went out among a party, and we were on part of the road, and the mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the adhan for prayer before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So we heard the voice of the mu'adhdhin while we were with him, so we shouted imitating him so that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would hear the voice. So he sent to us, and we stood before him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of you is the one whose voice I heard raised? So all the people pointed to me, and they spoke truth. So he sent them all and kept me. He said: So stand and call the adhan for prayer. So I stood, and there was nothing more hateful to me than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor than what he ordered me. So I stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me the calling himself, saying: Say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Then he said to me: Return and extend your voice, and say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; hasten to prayer, hasten to prayer; hasten to success, hasten to success; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah. Then he called me when I finished the calling, and gave me a purse in which was some silver; then he placed his hand on the forelock of Abu Mahdhurah, then passed it over his face from before him, then upon his liver, then the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached the navel of Abu Mahdhurah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah bless you and bless upon you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, command me to call in Makkah. He said: I have done. And everything there was in my heart of hatred for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went, and all of that returned as love for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I came to Attab ibn Asid, governor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I called the adhan with him for prayer by the order of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6756","6732 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Rummani al-Massisi, and Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal, they said: narrated to us Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah, he said: I heard my grandfather Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah mentioning that he heard Abu Mahdhurah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me the adhan letter by letter: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; hasten to prayer, hasten to prayer; hasten to success, hasten to success; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah."
"6757","6733 - Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Abi Mahdhurah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his grandfather Abu Mahdhurah, and he mentioned the like of it."
"6758","6734 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, informed me Uthman their freedman, from his father the shaykh, freedman of Abu Mahdhurah, and from Umm Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah, they said: Abu Mahdhurah said: I went out among ten youths with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Hunayn, and they were the most hateful of people to us; so they called the adhan, and we stood mocking them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me these youths. So he said: Call the adhan; so they called, and I was the last of them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, this is the one whose voice I heard; go and call for the people of Makkah, and say to Attab ibn Asid: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to call for the people of Makkah. And he wiped over his forelock and said: Say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, twice; then return and say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, twice; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, twice; hasten to prayer twice, hasten to success twice; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah. And when you call the first of Fajr, say: Prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep; and when you establish, say it twice: The prayer has been established - did you hear? So Abu Mahdhurah would not cut his forelock nor part it, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had wiped over it. Abu al-Qasim said: Uthman, from whom Ibn Jurayj narrated this hadith, is Uthman ibn al-Sa'ib, freedman of Banu Jumah."
"6759","6735 - Narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us al-Harith ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me the sunnah of the adhan. So he wiped the front of his head. He said: You say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; raising your voice with them; then you say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, lowering your voice with them; then you say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; hasten to prayer, hasten to prayer; hasten to success, hasten to success. Then if it is the Fajr prayer you say: Prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah."
"6760","6736 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us Dawud ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Qurashi, narrated to us Malik ibn Dinar, he said: I climbed to Ibn Abi Mahdhurah above the Sacred Mosque after he called, so I said to him: Inform me of the adhan of your father for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he said: He would begin and magnify, saying: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; hasten to prayer, hasten to prayer, once, once; then he would return and say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, until he came to the end of the adhan: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah."
"6761","6737 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah, narrated to us al-Hudhayl ibn Bilal, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mahdhurah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave to Banu Abd al-Muttalib the watering, and to Banu Abd al-Dar the veiling, and gave the adhan to us and to our freedmen."
"6762","6738 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Ja'far, from Abu Salman, from Abi Mahdhurah, he said: I used to call for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Fajr prayer, so I would say when I said in the first adhan: Hasten to success; prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep."
"6763","6739 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, they said: narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, narrated to us Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', he said: I heard Abu Mahdhurah saying: I was a young boy, so I called before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn; when I ended at hasten to prayer, hasten to success, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Append therein: Prayer is better than sleep."
"6764","6740 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Massisi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, he said: I asked Abu Mahdhurah: How did you call for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? What did you make the end of your adhan? He said: I would double the adhan, and double the iqamah, and make the end of my adhan: There is no god but Allah."
"6765","6741 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr, narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham, from Ammar ibn Zurayq, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Abi Mahdhurah, he said: The end of the adhan was: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah."
"6766","6742 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Azraq, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Khalid al-Bukhari, narrated to me my father, from Abu Hamzah, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, he said: I asked Abu Mahdhurah about the end of the adhan? So he said: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest."
"6767","6743 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, they said: narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Abi Mahdhurah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abi Mahdhurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mu'adhdhins are the trustees of the Muslims over their breaking of fast and their suhur."
"6768","6744 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, narrated to us Yahya, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Abi Mahdhurah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abi Mahdhurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you call Maghrib, hasten it with the sun, hastening."
"6769","6745 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah, he said: I heard my father saying: from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The time of Maghrib - hasten it with the sun."
"6770","6746 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Hudhayfah, narrated to us Ayyub ibn Thabit, from Safiyyah bint Majza'ah, that Abu Mahdhurah had a forelock in the front of his head; when he sat he would let it down so it reached the earth. So they said to him: Will you not shave it? So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over it with his hand, so I shall not shave it until I die; so he did not shave it until he died."
"6771","6747 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani, narrated to us Musa ibn Sahl al-Ramli, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Muhayriz, he said: I heard my father narrating, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Muhayriz, from his father, he said: I saw Abu Mahdhurah, and he had hair; so I said to him: Will you not take from your hair? So he said: I would not lighten hair over which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed his hand."
"6772","6748 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws ibn Khalid, he said: Whenever I came to Abu Mahdhurah he would ask me about a man, and whenever I came to the man he would ask me about Abu Mahdhurah. So I said to Abu Mahdhurah: When I come to you, you ask me about so-and-so, and when I come to him, he asks me about you? So he said: I and Abu Hurayrah and so-and-so were in a house, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last of you to die is in the Fire. So Abu Hurayrah died, then Abu Mahdhurah died, then the man died."
"6773","681 - Samurah ibn Jundub al-Fazari; he settled in Basrah and died there. Of his reports. 6749 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Harawi, narrated to us Hushaym, informed us Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from his father, that the mother of Samurah ibn Jundub: her husband died leaving her son Samurah, and she was a beautiful woman; so she came to Madinah and was sought in marriage. So she kept saying: I shall not marry a man except a man who guarantees for her the maintenance of her son Samurah until he comes of age. So a man of the Ansar married her on that condition, and she was with him among the Ansar. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would inspect the boys of the Ansar every year; whoever of them came of age, he sent him. So he inspected them one year, and a boy passed by him, so he sent him in the expedition; and Samurah was presented to him after him, so he rejected him. So Samurah said: O Messenger of Allah, you passed a boy and rejected me, and if he wrestled me I would throw him? He said: Then wrestle him. He said: So I threw him, so he passed me into the expedition."
"6774","What Samurah ibn Jundub narrated. Amir al-Sha'bi from Samurah ibn Jundub. 6750 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Amr ibn Marzuq, informed us Shu'bah, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Fajr prayer, then said: Is here anyone of Banu so-and-so? Your companion is detained at the gate of Paradise by a debt upon him."
"6775","6751 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Ibn al-Asbahani, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dalani, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in one of the prayers, then said: Who is here of the clan of so-and-so? Your companion has been held back from Paradise by a debt that was upon him; so either ransom him from the punishment of Allah, or surrender him."
"6776","6752 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us al-Fudayl ibn al-Husayn Abu Kamil al-Jahdari, narrated to us Abu Awanah, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: Is here anyone of Banu al-Najjar? So he called three times, none answering him; then a man answered him, so he said: Did you hear my call? He said: Yes. He said: So-and-so of you who died has been held back from Paradise because of the debt upon him; so if you wish, ransom him, and if you wish, surrender him to the punishment of Allah."
"6777","6753 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Musa, narrated to us Shayban, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and when he finished he said: Is here anyone of Banu al-Najjar? So he called three times, and a man answered him on the third; so he said: Did you hear my call? He said: Yes. He said: Your companion so-and-so has been held back from Paradise because of the debt that was upon him; so if you wish, ransom him from the punishment of Allah, and if you wish, surrender him."
"6778","6754 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, from Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the people one day and said: Is here anyone of Banu so-and-so? So the people were silent, and when he began them with something they were silent. Then he said: Is here anyone of Banu so-and-so? So a man of the people said: This is so-and-so. He said: Your companion is detained short of Paradise by his debt. So a man of the people said: His debt is upon me."
"6779","6755 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat al-Kufi, narrated to us Minjab ibn al-Harith, narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from al-Sha'bi, from Sam'an ibn Mushannaj, from Samurah ibn Jundub. [The report follows in the next narration.]"
"6780","(h) And narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Sa'id al-Warraq, narrated to us Sufyan al-Thawri, from his father, from al-Sha'bi, from Sam'an ibn Mushannaj, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a bier; when he finished he said: Is here anyone of the family of so-and-so? He said: So none stood until he said it three times; then a man stood and said: I, O Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What prevented you from standing the first two times? I only mentioned your name for good: So-and-so, a man who died, is held by his debt. He said: So I saw his family and those grieved by his affair; he said: So they paid what was upon him until nothing remained upon him."
"6781","6756 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Waki', from Sufyan, from his father, from al-Sha'bi, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it; and he did not mention Sam'an."
"6782","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Samurah. 6757 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Nusayr, (h) and narrated to us Yusuf al-Qadi, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Harb, (h) and narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil, narrated to us Ali ibn al-Ja'd, they said: narrated to us Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever narrates from me a hadith while he sees that it is a lie, then he is one of the liars."
"6783","Ali ibn Rabi'ah al-Walibi from Samurah. 6758 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, narrated to us Nu'aym ibn Hammad, narrated to us Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us Wiqa' ibn Iyas, from Ali ibn Rabi'ah, from Samurah ibn Jundub: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he addressed the people and forbade the dubba' and the muzaffat."
"6784","Maymun ibn Abi Shabib from Samurah. 6759 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, (h) and narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, narrated to us Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear these white garments, and shroud in them your dead, for they are purest and best."
"6785","6760 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, narrated to us al-Mas'udi, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white garments, for they are best and purest, and shroud in them your dead."
"6786","6761 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us Qays ibn al-Rabi', from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white garments, for they are best and purest, and shroud in them your dead."
"6787","6762 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawwazi, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Hammad Sajjadah, narrated to us Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purest of your garments are white, so wear them and shroud in them your dead."
"6788","Abdullah ibn Buraydah from Samurah ibn Jundub. 6763 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Muslim ibn Ibrahim and Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us Hammam, narrated to us Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Samurah ibn Jundub: that a woman died in childbed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over her, and he stood at her middle."
"6789","6764 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak and Yazid ibn Harun, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Samurah ibn Jundub: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a woman, and he stood at her middle."
"6790","6765 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Ansari, narrated to us Shabbabah ibn Sawwar, narrated to us Shu'bah, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Samurah ibn Jundub: that a woman died in pregnancy, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over her, and he stood at her middle."
"6791","Zayd ibn Uqbah al-Fazari from Samurah ibn Jundub. 6766 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, narrated to us Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begging is scratching by which a man scratches his face; so whoever wishes keeps his face, and whoever wishes leaves it."
"6792","6767 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, narrated to us Shu'bah, (h) and narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qitrani, they said: narrated to us Amr ibn Marzuq, informed us Shu'bah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begging is but scratches by which a man scratches his face; so whoever wishes keeps his face, and whoever wishes leaves it, except that he ask one in authority or in a matter from which he finds no escape."
"6793","6768 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Waki', from Sufyan, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These beggings are scratching by which one of you scratches his face, except that a man ask one in authority, or a matter he must have."
"6794","6769 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Arim Abu al-Nu'man, narrated to us Abu Awanah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These beggings are scratching by which a man scratches his face, except that he ask one in authority or in a matter from which he finds no escape."
"6795","6770 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Musa, narrated to us Shayban, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Zayd ibn Uqbah al-Fazari, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: These beggings are but scratching by which a man scratches his face; so whoever wishes keeps his face, and whoever wishes leaves it, except that a man ask one in authority or in a matter he must have."
"6796","6771 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Jarir, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Uqbah, or so-and-so ibn Uqbah al-Fazari, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: These beggings are but scratching by which a man scratches his face; so whoever wishes keeps his face, and whoever wishes leaves it, except that a man ask one in authority or in a matter he must have."
"6797","6772 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us al-Rabi' ibn Yahya al-Ushnani, narrated to us Za'idah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: These beggings are but scratching by which a man scratches his face."
"6798","6773 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, narrated to us Yahya al-Himmani, narrated to us Hushaym, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"6799","6774 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Waki', from Sufyan, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"6800","6775 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, narrated to us Mis'ar, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from one who narrated to him, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Jumu'ah: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"6801","6776 - Narrated to us Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, (h) and narrated to us Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, narrated to us Asim ibn Ali, they said: narrated to us al-Mas'udi, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"6802","6777 - Narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, narrated to us Abu Mu'awiyah, from al-Hajjaj, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, in the first, and in the second: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"6803","6778 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi, narrated to us Hibban ibn Musa and Suwayd ibn Nasr, they said: narrated to us Ibn al-Mubarak, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, in the first, and in the second: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"6804","6779 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us al-Rabi' ibn Yahya al-Ushnani, narrated to us Shu'bah, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Zayd ibn Uqbah, from Samurah ibn Jundub: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite on Friday in the Jumu'ah prayer: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"6805","6780 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Umar ibn Awn, narrated to us Abu Bakr al-Dahiri, from Mis'ar, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from his father, from Samurah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to cut the thong between his fingers."
"6806","6781 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, (h) and narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us Musaddad, they said: narrated to us Abu Mu'awiyah, from al-Hajjaj, from Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Uqbah, from his father, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loses goods and finds them in the hand of a man in their very form, he is most entitled to them, and the buyer returns to the seller for the price."
"6807","6782 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, from Abu Shaybah, from Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Uqbah, from his father, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two months do not complete sixty days."
"6808","6783 - Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Usayd al-Asbahani, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Razi, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Idris, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Ala', from Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Uqbah, from his father, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Two months do not complete sixty days."
"6809","Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr from Samurah. 6784 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qitrani, they said: narrated to us Amr ibn Marzuq, narrated to us Shu'bah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, from Samurah ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best you treat yourselves with is cupping."
"6810","6785 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us Arim Abu al-Nu'man, narrated to us Abu Awanah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called a cupper, and he cupped him with a horn and the cut of a blade; so a Bedouin of Banu Fazarah saw him and said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you let this one cut your flesh? He said: Do you know what this cupping is? And it is the best you treat yourselves with."
"6811","6786 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to me my father, narrated to us Zuhayr, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, narrated to me Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, from Samurah, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he called a cupper and ordered him to cup him; so he brought out cupping vessels of horns, and attached them to him, then cut him with the edge of a blade, and poured the blood into a vessel with him. Then a man of Banu Fazarah entered upon him and said: What is this, O Messenger of Allah? Why do you enable this one over your skin to cut it? So he said: This is cupping. He said: It is the best men treat themselves with."
"6812","6787 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Musa, narrated to us Shayban, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"6813","6788 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, narrated to us Abu Awanah, (h) and narrated to us Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri, narrated to us Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Amr, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn ibn Qabisah, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: A Bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was delivering the sermon, and interrupted his sermon; so he turned to him while he was on his right and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about lizards? He said: A community of the Children of Israel was transformed; Allah knows in which beasts they were transformed."
"6814","6789 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah, narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Musa, narrated to us Shayban, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, from Samurah, he said: A Bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What do you say about lizards? So he said: A community of the Children of Israel was transformed, so Allah knows which beasts they were transformed into."
"6815","6790 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir, narrated to us Affan, narrated to us Abu Awanah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, from Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"6816","Al-Rabi ibn Umayla from Samura ibn Jundub. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Zuhayr from Mansur from Hilal ibn Yasaf from al-Rabi ibn Umayla from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved speech to Allah, Almighty and Exalted, is four: there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great, and glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah; it does not harm you with which of them you begin."
"6817","Narrated Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi from Abu Mamar al-Muqad, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani, both saying: Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Juhada from Mansur from Umara ibn Umayr from al-Rabi ibn Umayla, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The most beloved speech to Allah, Almighty and Exalted, is: glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great; it does not harm you with which of them you begin."
"6818","Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Zuhayr from Mansur from Hilal ibn Yasaf from al-Rabi ibn Umayla from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not name your boy Yasar, nor Rabah, nor Najih, nor Aflah, for you will say: Is he there? And he will not be there, so it will be said: No; they are only four, and do not add to them."
"6819","Narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi from Abu Mamar al-Muqad, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from Yahya al-Himmani, both saying: Abd al-Warith narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Juhada from Mansur from Umara ibn Umayr from al-Rabi ibn Umayla from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not name your slave Rabah, nor Najih, nor Aflah, nor Yasar."
"6820","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from Yahya al-Himmani from Mutamir from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to give our slaves four names: Nafi, Aflah, Rabah, and Yasar."
"6821","Thalaba ibn Ibad al-Abdi from Samura. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym from Sufyan from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Abu Ibad from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them during the eclipse of the sun, and no voice of his could be heard."
"6822","Narrated Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi from Hibban ibn Musa, and narrated Abu Sad Yahya ibn Mansur al-Harawi from Suwayd ibn Nasr, both saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Sufyan from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Thalaba ibn Ibad al-Abdi, who said: I heard Samura ibn Jundub in his sermon saying: While I and a boy of the Ansar were shooting at a target, the sun rose, and to the eye of the beholder it was about two or three spears high, then it brightened until it shone as though it were a tannuma plant; one of us said to his companion: Come with us, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will surely speak to us about the eclipse of the sun concerning his umma. We reached the mosque, and the mosque was full and crowded, and that coincided with the coming out of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he went forward and prayed with the people while we were behind him; he stood with us as long as he ever stood with us in a prayer, and we could not hear any voice from him, then he bowed with us as long as he ever bowed with us in a prayer, and we could not hear any voice from him, then he prostrated with us with the longest prostration, and we could not hear any voice from him, then he did likewise in the second rak'a, and the clearing of the sun coincided with the sitting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then he finished, praised Allah and extolled Him, bore witness that there is no god but Allah, and bore witness that he is His servant and Messenger, then said: O people, I am but a human Messenger; I remind you by Allah, if you know that I have fallen short in conveying anything of the messages of my Lord, then tell me, for I have conveyed the messages of my Lord as they ought to be conveyed; and if I have conveyed the messages of my Lord, then tell me? They said: We bear witness that you have conveyed the messages of your Lord, advised your umma, and fulfilled what was upon you. Then he said: To proceed, some men claim that the eclipse of this sun and this moon, or the departure of the stars from their rising places, is due to the death of great men of the earth, and they have lied; rather, they are signs among the signs of Allah by which He admonishes His servants, to see who among them will show repentance because of them; I have been shown, in this place of mine while praying, what you will meet in your worldly life and your Hereafter; the Hour will not come until thirty liars come out, the last of them the one-eyed Dajjal, with his left eye effaced as though it were the eye of Abu Tihya, an old man of the Ansar between him and the chamber of Aisha; when he comes out he will claim that he is Allah; whoever believes in him and affirms him, no past good deed of his will benefit him, and whoever disbelieves in him and denies him will not be punished for any past deed; he will appear over the whole earth except the Sanctuary and Bayt al-Maqdis; the believers will be besieged in Bayt al-Maqdis with a severe siege and suffer severe hardship. Al-Aswad ibn Qays said: And I think he said: Isa son of Maryam (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will come upon them in the morning, and Allah will rout him and his troops, until the trunk of a wall and the branch of a tree will call out to the believer, saying: Here is a disbeliever hiding behind me, come and kill him; that will not happen until you see things of your affair that weigh heavily upon you, until you ask one another: Did your Prophet mention anything of this? And until mountains move from their places; then upon that will be the seizure, the seizure. Ibn al-Mubarak said: Meaning death."
"6823","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani, both saying: Abu Awana narrated to us from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Thalaba ibn Ibad, who said: I witnessed Samura ibn Jundub while he was preaching, and he mentioned in his sermon a narration from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: While I and a boy of the Ansar were shooting at two targets of ours at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the sun rose, and to the eye of the beholder it was a spear or two spears from the horizon, then it darkened until it shone as though it were a tannuma plant; one of them said to his companion: Let us go to the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for by Allah, he will surely speak today about this sun concerning his umma. We hastened to the mosque and found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as he came out to the people; he went forward and prayed; he stood with us as long as he ever stood with us in any prayer, and we could not hear any voice from him, then he bowed with us as long as he ever bowed with us in any prayer, and we could not hear any voice from him, then he prostrated with us as long as he ever prostrated with us in any prayer, and we could not hear any voice from him, then he stood and prayed with us another rak'a like it, then sat, and his sitting coincided with the clearing of the sun; he gave the salutation and finished, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, I remind you by Allah, if you know that I have conveyed the message of my Lord, then tell me, and if you know that I have fallen short in conveying anything of the message of my Lord, then tell me. They said: We bear witness that you have conveyed the message of your Lord, advised your umma, and fulfilled what was upon you. Then he said: To proceed, some men claim that the eclipse of this sun and the eclipse of this moon, and the departure of the stars from their rising places, is due to the death of great men of the people of the earth, and they have lied; rather, they are the signs of Allah, by which He admonishes His servants, to see who among them will show repentance because of them; and by Allah, I have seen, since I stood praying, what you will meet of the affair of your worldly life and your Hereafter; and by Allah, the Hour will not come until thirty liars come out, the last of them the one-eyed Dajjal, with his left eye effaced as though it were the eye of Abu Tihya, an old man of the Ansar between him and the chamber of Aisha; when he comes out he will claim that he is Allah; whoever believes in him and affirms him, no past good deed of his will benefit him, and whoever disbelieves in him and fights him will not be punished for any past deed of his; he will appear over the whole earth except the Sanctuary and Bayt al-Maqdis; he will drive the people to Bayt al-Maqdis, and they will be besieged with a severe siege. He said: And I think he said: Isa son of Maryam will come upon them in the morning and kill him and his troops, until a stone or the trunk of a wall will call out: O Muslim, or O believer, here is a disbeliever hiding behind me, come and kill him; that will not happen until you see grave matters whose seriousness weighs heavily upon you, and you ask one another: Did your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention anything of them to you? Then he said: Upon the heels of that will be the seizure."
"6824","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail, and narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father, both saying: Zuhayr narrated to us from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Thalaba ibn Ibad al-Abdi, who said: I witnessed a sermon one day by Samura ibn Jundub, and he mentioned in his sermon from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: While I and a boy of the Ansar were shooting at two targets of ours at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the sun was two or three spears high to the eye of the beholders from the horizon, it darkened until it shone as though it were a tannuma plant; one of us said to his companion: Let us go to the mosque, for by Allah, the affair of this sun will surely bring about a new matter for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning his umma. I went to the mosque, and it was crowded, meaning full; we found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as he came out to the people; he went forward and stood with us as long as he ever stood with us in any prayer, and we could not hear any voice from him, then he bowed as long as he ever bowed with us in any prayer, and we could not hear any voice from him, then he prostrated as long as he ever prostrated with us in any prayer, and we could not hear any voice from him, then he did likewise in the second rak'a, and the clearing of the sun coincided with his sitting in the second rak'a; he gave the salutation, then praised Allah, extolled Him, bore witness that there is no god but He, and that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger, then said: O people, I am but a human Messenger, so I adjure you by Allah, if you know that I have fallen short in conveying anything of the messages of my Lord, then tell me, for I have conveyed the messages of my Lord as they ought to be conveyed? And if you know that I have conveyed the messages of my Lord, then tell me? The people stood and said: We bear witness that you have conveyed the messages of your Lord, advised your umma, and fulfilled what was upon you. Then they fell silent. Then he said: To proceed, some men claim that the eclipse of this sun and the eclipse of this moon, and the departure of these stars from their rising places, is due to the death of great men of the people of the earth, and they have lied; rather, they are signs among the signs of Allah, Almighty and Exalted, by which He admonishes His servants, to see who among them will show repentance because of them; and by Allah, I have seen, since I stood praying, what you will meet in the affair of your worldly life and your Hereafter; and by Allah, the Hour will not come until thirty liars come out, the last of them the one-eyed Dajjal, with his left eye effaced as though it were the eye of Abu Tihya, an old man of the Ansar at that time between him and the chamber of Aisha; when he comes out he will claim that he is Allah; whoever believes in him, affirms him, and follows him, no past good deed of his will benefit him, and whoever disbelieves in him and denies him will not be punished for any past deed of his; he will appear over the whole earth except the Sanctuary and Bayt al-Maqdis; he will besiege the Muslims in Bayt al-Maqdis, and they will suffer severe hardship; then Allah will destroy him and his troops, until the trunk of a wall and the root of a tree will say: O believer, or O Muslim, here is a disbeliever, come and kill him; that will not happen until you see grave matters whose seriousness weighs heavily upon you, then you ask one another: Did your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention anything of them to you? And until mountains move from their places; then upon the heels of that will be the seizure. And he closed his fingers and gestured right and left. Then I witnessed a sermon by Samura in which he mentioned this narration, and he did not put forward a word nor delay one from its place."
"6825","Al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Basri from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him. Chapter: Qatada from al-Hasan. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym and Muslim ibn Ibrahim, both saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged in favor of neighborhood."
"6826","Narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar, Abu Khalifa, and Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Sawra al-Baghdadi, who said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us from Shuba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of a house has more right to the house and the land than anyone else."
"6827","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz from Abu Umar al-Hawdi from Hammam from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of a house has more right to the house than anyone else."
"6828","Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from Isa ibn Yunus from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of a house has more right to preemption of the house."
"6829","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Daqiqi al-Tustari from al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan from Yahya ibn Fudayl from Hasan ibn Salih from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The neighbor of a house has more right to the house."
"6830","Narrated al-Muammil ibn Muhammad ibn Sayyar al-Shirazi from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Muthanna al-Bahili from Salim ibn Nuh from Umar ibn Amir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged in favor of neighborhood."
"6831","Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Bazzar al-Tustari from Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad from my father from Umar ibn Ibrahim from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of a house has more right to the house."
"6832","Narrated Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Abu Dawud from Hisham al-Dastuwai from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The neighbor of a house has more right to the house."
"6833","Chapter. Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Asim ibn Ali from Shuba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him."
"6834","Narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi al-Qadi from Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani from Hushaym from Shuba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him."
"6835","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Hudba ibn Khalid from Hammad ibn Salama from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him."
"6836","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad, and narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Khalid ibn Khidash, both saying: Abu Awana narrated to us from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him."
"6837","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz from Said ibn Amir from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him."
"6838","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muhammad ibn al-Minhal from Yazid ibn Zuray from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him."
"6839","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Daqiqi al-Tustari from al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan from Yahya ibn Fudayl from al-Hasan ibn Salih from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him."
"6840","Narrated Bakr ibn Ahmad ibn Sadawayh al-Tahi al-Basri from Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya and Nasr ibn Ali, both saying: Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us from Hisham al-Dastuwai from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him, and whoever castrates his slave, we will castrate him."
"6841","Narrated Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Muadh ibn Hisham from my father from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever castrates his slave, we will castrate him, and whoever mutilates his nose, we will mutilate him."
"6842","Chapter. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz, both saying: Abu Amir al-Hawdi narrated to us, and narrated Abu Khalifa and Yusuf al-Qadi, both saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, both saying: Hammam narrated to us from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday, that suffices, and it is a blessing, and whoever bathes, then bathing is better."
"6843","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Muhammad ibn al-Minhal from Yazid ibn Zuray from Shuba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday, that suffices, and it is a blessing, and whoever bathes, then bathing is better."
"6844","Narrated Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Said ibn Sufyan al-Jahdari from Shuba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"6845","Narrated Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath from Abu Awana from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution, that suffices, and it is a blessing, and whoever bathes, then bathing is better."
"6846","Chapter. Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib from Affan from Hammam from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his caller on a cold night to call out: Prayer in the dwellings."
"6847","Narrated Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Muadh ibn Hisham from my father from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: Rain befell us while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he called out: Prayer in the dwellings."
"6848","Chapter. Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza al-Dimashqi from Abu al-Jumahir from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to guard the prayers and the middle prayer, and informed us that it is the Asr prayer."
"6849","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Aban ibn Yazid from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, concerning His saying, Almighty and Exalted: Guard the prayers and the middle prayer, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the Asr prayer."
"6850","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yazid ibn Zuray, and narrated Musa ibn Harun from Abu Ghassan al-Mismai from Khalid ibn al-Harith, both saying: Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The middle prayer is the Asr prayer."
"6851","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq al-Razi from Abu Dawud from Shuba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The middle prayer is the Asr prayer."
"6852","Chapter. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Ibn Aisha, both saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The boy is pledged for his aqiqa."
"6853","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz from Abu Umar al-Hawdi from Hammam from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every boy is held in pledge for his aqiqa; an animal is slaughtered for him on the seventh day, and his head is shaved."
"6854","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami, both saying: Sallam ibn Abi Muti narrated to us from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every boy is pledged for his aqiqa, and an animal is slaughtered for him on his seventh day, and his head is shaved and he is named."
"6855","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Jabir al-Muharibi from Yahya ibn Yala ibn al-Harith from my father from Ghaylan ibn Jami from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every boy is held in pledge for his aqiqa; an animal is slaughtered for him on his seventh day, and he is named, and his head is shaved."
"6856","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, and narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti from Wahb ibn Baqiyya from Yazid ibn Zuray from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every boy is held in pledge for his aqiqa; an animal is slaughtered for him on his seventh day, his head is smeared, and he is named."
"6857","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Muhammad ibn Bishr from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The boy is held in pledge for his aqiqa; the aqiqa is offered for him on his seventh day, and his head is shaved and he is named."
"6858","Chapter. Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Hisham al-Dastuwai from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The two traders retain the option as long as they have not parted, unless their sale is with a stipulated option."
"6859","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz from Said ibn Amir from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The two traders retain the option as long as they have not parted."
"6860","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz from Abu Umar al-Hawdi from Hammam ibn Yahya from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two traders retain the option as long as they have not parted, and each of them takes what he is pleased with of the transaction."
"6861","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Abu Kamil al-Jahdari from Abu Awana from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two traders retain the option as long as they have not parted."
"6862","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani from Zayd ibn Akhram from Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith from Shuba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The two traders retain the option as long as they have not parted."
"6863","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Sulami al-Ghazzal from Abu Hisham al-Rifai from Salim ibn Nuh from Umar ibn Amir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two traders retain the option as long as they have not parted."
"6864","Chapter. Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Hisham al-Dastuwai from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whichever woman is married off by two guardians, she belongs to the first of them; and whichever man sells a sale to two men, it belongs to the first of them."
"6865","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi, and narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar from Ubayd Allah ibn Aisha, and narrated Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath, who said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two men marry off a woman, the first is more entitled; and when two men purchase a transaction, the first is more entitled."
"6866","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz from Abu Umar al-Hawdi from Hammam from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a woman is married to two husbands, she belongs to the first of them; and when a sale is sold to two men, it belongs to the first of them."
"6867","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Daqiqi al-Tustari from al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan from Yahya ibn Fudayl from Hasan ibn Salih from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whichever woman two guardians marry off together, she belongs to the first of them; and whichever man sells a sale to two men together, it belongs to the first of them."
"6868","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Jabala from Sallam ibn Abi Muti from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two guardians marry off, she belongs to the first of them; and when two authorizing agents sell, it belongs to the first of them."
"6869","Chapter. Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi and Abu Khalifa, both saying: Abu al-Walid narrated to us from Hammam from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The umra gift is permissible."
"6870","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, and narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, both saying: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The umra gift is permissible."
"6871","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Muhammad ibn Bishr from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The umra gift is permissible for its people."
"6872","Chapter. Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Massisi from Hassan ibn Hilal from Aban ibn Yazid from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling an animal for an animal on credit."
"6873","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib from Surayj ibn al-Numan, and narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Asim ibn Ali, and narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi, who said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling an animal for an animal on credit."
"6874","Narrated Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar from Yazid ibn Harun from Said ibn Abi Aruba, and narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad, and narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi, both saying: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, both saying: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, and narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Shihab ibn Abbad from Muhammad ibn Bishr, both saying: Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling an animal for an animal on credit."
"6875","Narrated al-Muammil ibn Muhammad ibn Sayyar al-Shirazi from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Muthanna al-Bahili from Salim ibn Nuh from Umar ibn Amir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling an animal for an animal on credit."
"6876","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa from Hasan ibn Salih from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling an animal for an animal on credit."
"6877","Chapter. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal and Muslim ibn Ibrahim, and narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib from Surayj ibn al-Numan, and narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar from Ubayd Allah ibn Aisha, and narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath, who said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever owns a relative within the prohibited degrees, he is free."
"6878","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari from Affan, and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal from Hammad ibn Salama from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Quran was revealed in three readings."
"6879","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib and al-Hasan ibn al-Mutawakkil, both saying: Surayj ibn al-Numan al-Jawhari narrated to us from al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Attend Friday prayer and draw near to the imam, for a man may have a station in Paradise, then stay back from Friday, and so be kept back from it."
"6880","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar from al-Hasan ibn Bishr from al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan has kohl and a linctus; when he applies his kohl to a man, his eyes sleep from remembrance, and when he gives him his linctus to lick, his tongue becomes foul with evil."
"6881","Narrated Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan al-Baghdadi al-Basri from al-Hasan ibn Bishr from al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People who were with me will come to me, and when they raise their heads to me they will be snatched away from me, so I will say: My Lord, my companions, my companions? And it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"6882","Narrated Abu Zayd al-Hawti from Abu al-Yaman from Ufayr ibn Mabad from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until mountains move from their places, and you see grave matters that you never used to see."
"6883","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Hisham al-Dastuwai from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse one another with the curse of Allah, nor with the anger of Allah, nor with the Fire."
"6884","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi from Ahmad ibn Jafar from my father from Ibrahim ibn Tahman from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse one another with the curse of Allah, nor with the anger of Allah, nor with the Fire."
"6885","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Amr ibn Awn from Hushaym from Musa ibn al-Saib from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever finds the very item of his property, he has more right to it, and the seller pursues the one who sold to him."
"6886","Narrated Uthman ibn Khalid ibn Amr al-Sulafi al-Himsi from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Himsi from Ismail ibn Ayyash from Nafi ibn Amir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever recognizes his property, let him take it, and the seller seeks his sale wherever it is."
"6887","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Umar al-Hawdi from Murajja ibn Raja, and narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muhammad ibn al-Minhal from Yazid ibn Zuray, and narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yahya, and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Muhammad ibn Bishr, all from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand is responsible for what it takes until it delivers it."
"6888","Chapter. Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi, both saying: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us from Yazid ibn Zuray from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever encloses something, it belongs to him."
"6889","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni al-Tustari from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr from Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr from Huraym ibn Sufyan al-Bajali from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever encloses land with a wall, it belongs to him."
"6890","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani from Abu Masud Ahmad ibn al-Furat from Abu Dawud from Shuba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever encloses a wall, it belongs to him."
"6891","Narrated Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Massisi from Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn from Abbad ibn al-Awwam from Umar ibn Ibrahim from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever encloses land with a wall, it belongs to him."
"6892","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Jabala from Sallam ibn Abi Muti from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever encloses a wall around land, it belongs to him."
"6893","Chapter. Narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti from Wahb ibn Baqiyya from Khalid, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Wasiti from my father from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever overcomes water, it belongs to him. And Wahb ibn Baqiyya said: He has more right to it."
"6894","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi from Abd Allah ibn Yazid ibn Rashid al-Dimashqi from Sadaqa ibn Abd Allah from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a townsman to sell for a Bedouin."
"6895","Narrated Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, both saying: Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us from Kahmas ibn al-Minhal from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling years ahead."
"6896","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi from Yazid ibn Zuray from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Sam is the father of the Arabs, Ham the father of the Abyssinians, and Japheth the father of the Romans."
"6897","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza al-Dimashqi from Abu al-Jumahir from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The children of Nuh are Sam, Japheth, and Ham."
"6898","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Hisham ibn Ammar from al-Walid ibn Muslim from Khulayd ibn Dalaj and Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The children of Nuh are three: Sam, Japheth, and Ham."
"6899","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, and narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr, both saying: Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The warranty of a slave is three days."
"6900","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muhammad ibn al-Minhal from Yazid ibn Zuray from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan, who said: Samura said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a pause when he said the takbir, and a pause when he finished reciting the sura; Imran ibn Husayn criticized him for that, so they wrote to Ubayy ibn Kab about it, and Ubayy wrote: Samura spoke the truth. And he says: Samura memorized the narration from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6901","Narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar from Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Samina from Yazid ibn Zuray, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Dawud ibn Rushayd from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, both saying: Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pause twice."
"6902","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Mamari from Yusuf ibn Hammad al-Mani from Abd al-Ala from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes upon grazing livestock, if he sees its owner there let him ask his permission; if he permits him, let him milk and drink, and if there is no one there, let him call out three times; if someone comes, let him ask his permission, otherwise let him milk and drink, but let him not carry away."
"6903","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Attar from Sayf ibn Ubayd Allah from Sarrar ibn Mujashshir from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you passes by livestock, let him call out three times; if anyone answers him, well and good, otherwise let him milk and drink."
"6904","Narrated Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi and Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Massisi, both saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal al-Dimashqi narrated to us from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The severest regrets of the children of Adam are over three: a man who had a beautiful wife, and she bore him a boy, then she died, and he has nothing with which to hire a wet nurse for his son; a man who was on a horse in a raid, and saw the spoils, and raced his companions to it, until when he drew near it his horse fell and died, while his companions reached the spoils and divided them; and a man who had crops and a water camel, and when his crops ripened and were ready for harvest, his water camel died, and he has nothing with which to buy a camel."
"6905","Narrated Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi and Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Massisi, both saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who comes early to Friday is like one who offers a camel, then like one who offers a cow, then like one who offers a sheep, then like one who offers a chicken."
"6906","Narrated Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi and Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Massisi, both saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every Prophet has a pool over which they vie, which of them has more comers; and I hope to be the one of them with the most comers."
"6907","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri from Abu al-Jumahir from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked the Muhajirun and the Ansar to be next to him in prayer, so that they would learn from him."
"6908","Narrated Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi from Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to be moderate in prostration and not to crouch."
"6909","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri from Abu al-Jumahir from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to be moderate in prostration and not to crouch."
"6910","Narrated Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Massisi from al-Hasan ibn Bishr from al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Garden of Firdaws is the hill of the highest Paradise, which is its middle and its best."
"6911","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri from Abu al-Jumahir from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Firdaws is the hill of Paradise, its highest and its middle, and from it the rivers of Paradise gush forth."
"6912","Narrated Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar from my father from my grandfather from Said ibn Bashir, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Makhlad ibn Malik from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud al-Harrani from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the Bedouins stand behind the Muhajirun and the Ansar, so that they follow them in prayer."
"6913","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqa al-Baghdadi from al-Haytham ibn Marwan al-Dimashqi from Marwan ibn Muhammad from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Adam grows old, but two things in him grow young: greed for wealth, and long life."
"6914","Narrated Ishaq ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati from Hisham ibn Ammar from al-Walid ibn Muslim from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the people of the Fire are those whom the Fire takes up to their ankles, and up to their knees, and up to their waists, and up to their collarbones."
"6915","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi from Muhammad ibn Musaffa from al-Walid ibn Muslim from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us, when the imam gives the salutation, to return it to him."
"6916","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutayba al-Asqalani from Muhammad ibn Khalaf al-Asqalani from Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the imam says: Not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray, say: Amen; Allah will answer you."
"6917","Narrated Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani from Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz from Shuba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, and Shuba from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Zayd ibn Uqba from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begging is scratches and gashes on a man's face, unless a man asks his father, or the ruler over him."
"6918","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Ali ibn al-Madini, and narrated Musa ibn Harun from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from Muadh ibn Hisham from my father from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade celibacy; then Qatada recited: And We sent messengers before you and made for them wives and offspring."
"6919","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad Arara from Muadh ibn Hisham, who said: I found in the book of my father from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The day of the greater Hajj is the day Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, performed Hajj with the people."
"6920","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, Abu Khalifa, and Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini, who said: Shadh ibn al-Fayyad narrated to us from Umar ibn Ibrahim from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hawwa would have no child live for her, so Satan said to her: Name him Abd al-Harith, for he will live; so they named him, and that was from the inspiration of Satan and his command. Then she carried a light pregnancy that did not show, and she walked with it; when her pregnancy became apparent."
"6921","Narrated Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, and narrated Abu Khalifa and Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji, both saying: Muhammad ibn Yasar narrated to us, both saying: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us from Umar ibn Ibrahim from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is tormented by the weeping of the living."
"6922","Narrated Ahmad ibn Ismail al-Adawi al-Basri from Amr ibn Marzuq from Imran al-Qattan from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Establish prayer, give zakat, perform Hajj and Umra, and stay upright; you will be kept upright."
"6923","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from my father and Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani, who said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us from Imran al-Qattan from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man should not propose over the proposal of his brother."
"6924","Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti from my father, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Hisham ibn Ammar, both saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the imam gives the salutation, return it to him."
"6925","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Amr ibn Awn from Hushaym from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Uthman ibn Said al-Madani from al-Minhal ibn Khalifa from al-Hajjaj from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Kill the aged men of the polytheists, and spare their youths."
"6926","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Abu Muawiya from al-Hajjaj from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill the aged men of the polytheists, and spare their youths."
"6927","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi from my father from al-Walid ibn Muslim from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill the aged men of the polytheists, and spare their youths."
"6928","Narrated Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi from Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath from my father from al-Hajjaj from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The battle cry of the Muhajirun was O Abd Allah, and the battle cry of the Ansar was O Abd al-Rahman."
"6929","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Sahl ibn Uthman from Yahya ibn Abi Zaida from al-Hajjaj from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed for rain, would say: O Allah, send down in our land its adornment and its tranquility."
"6930","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Asbahani and al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah al-Kharaqi al-Baghdadi, both saying: Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us from Ishaq ibn Idris from Hammam from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not dwell with the polytheists, nor gather with them; whoever dwells with them or gathers with them is one of them."
"6931","Narrated Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi and Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji, both saying: Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah al-Kharaqi from Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi, both saying: Abd al-Ala ibn al-Qasim narrated to us from Hammam from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to give salutation to our right, and that some of us greet others."
"6932","Narrated Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Harrani from Uthman ibn Miqsam from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to greet our women, and that some of us return the greeting to others."
"6933","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Ubayd al-Ijl, both saying: Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Bukhari narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Bilal from Hammam from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman should not be married along with her paternal aunt, nor along with her maternal aunt."
"6934","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi, and narrated Abdan from Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi, both saying: Yala ibn Abbad narrated to us from Hammam from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"6935","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Yunus al-Ahwazi al-Katib from Rashid ibn Sallam al-Ahwazi from Yala ibn Abbad from Hammam from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to cut a strap between two fingers."
"6936","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji, both saying: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us from Nuh ibn Qays from his brother Khalid ibn Qays from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever misses Friday prayer, let him give a dinar in charity; if he does not find one, then half a dinar."
"6937","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki, both saying: Muhammad ibn Muawiya al-Naysaburi narrated to us from Sallam ibn Abi Muti from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lineage is wealth, and nobility is piety."
"6938","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Ali ibn al-Madini, and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, both saying: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Sallam ibn Abi Muti from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lineage is wealth, and nobility is piety."
"6939","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Jabala from Sallam ibn Abi Muti from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who is consulted is trusted."
"6940","Narrated Abu Ubayda Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Jabala from Sallam ibn Abi Muti from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The place of the lower garment is the shin, and the lower garment has no right over the ankles."
"6941","Narrated Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad from my father from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Umar ibn Musa from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: This day I have perfected for you your religion, and completed upon you My favor, and approved for you Islam as religion was revealed on the day of Arafa, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing at Arafa on a Friday."
"6942","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Muhammad ibn Humayd from Kinana ibn Jabala from Ibrahim ibn Tahman from al-Hajjaj from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays Fajr is under the protection of Allah; let Allah not demand anything of you from His protection."
"6943","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj al-Askari from Sulayman ibn Umar ibn Khalid al-Raqqi from my father from al-Khalil ibn Murra, and narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Salama ibn Shabib from Yazid ibn Abi Hakim from Ibrahim ibn Tahman from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, both from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will come out, and he is blind in his left eye, in which there is a thick growth; he will cure the blind and the leper and give life to the dead, and will say to the people: I am your lord; whoever says: You are my lord, has lied grievously, and whoever says: My Lord is Allah, until he dies upon that, has been protected from the trial of the Dajjal. And the wording is that of al-Khalil ibn Murra."
"6944","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj from al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzaz from Rawh ibn Ubada from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will come out, and he is blind in his left eye, over which there is a thick growth; he will cure the blind and the leper and give life to the dead, and will say to the people: I am your lord; whoever says: You are my lord, has been tried, and whoever says: My Lord is Allah, until he dies upon that, has been protected from the trial of the Dajjal, and there is no trial upon him; he will remain on earth as long as Allah wills, then Isa son of Maryam will come from the direction of the west, affirming Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and will kill the Dajjal; it is but the coming of the Hour."
"6945","Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Said ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari from Khalaf ibn al-Walid from Ayyub ibn Utba from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of a house has more right to the house."
"6946","Yunus ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, and narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir from Affan, both saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us from Yunus ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: It is near that Allah will fill your hands with non-Arabs, then make them lions who do not flee; they will kill your fighters and consume your spoils."
"6947","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki from Hafs ibn Umar from Muadh ibn Muhammad al-Hudhali from Yunus ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who flees from death is like the likeness of the fox, whom the earth demands a debt from; he kept running until, when he grew weary and panted, he entered his hole; the earth said to him: O fox, my debt? So he came out, panting heavily, and remained so until his neck was severed, and he died."
"6948","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Ahmad ibn Hubab al-Massisi from Isa ibn Yunus from Shuba from Yunus ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of a house has more right to the house."
"6949","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Ahmad ibn Tariq al-Wabishi from Yusuf ibn Atiyya al-Saffar from Yunus ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two guardians marry off, the first is more entitled; and when two sellers sell, the first is more entitled."
"6950","Narrated Ali ibn Bayan al-Mutarriz and Abd Allah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi, both saying: Abu Mamar Salih ibn Harb narrated to us from Sallam ibn Abi Khubza from Yunus ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to pray at night, little or much, and to make that witr."
"6951","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad from Khalid ibn Yahya from Yunus ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday, that suffices, and it is a blessing, and whoever bathes, then bathing is better."
"6952","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Muhammad ibn Humayd from Harun ibn al-Mughira from Abu Jafar al-Razi from Yunus ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him."
"6953","Matar al-Warraq from al-Hasan. Narrated Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza al-Dimashqiyan, both saying: Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us from Said ibn Bashir from Matar al-Warraq from al-Hasan from Samura, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed for rain, would supplicate: O Allah, place in our land its blessing, its adornment, and its tranquility."
"6954","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Ali ibn al-Madini from Muadh ibn Hisham from my father from Matar from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the caravans until they reach the market."
"6955","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Ali ibn al-Madini, and narrated Abd Allah ibn Najiya from Shabab al-Usfuri, both saying: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us from my father from Matar al-Warraq from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A townsman should not sell for a Bedouin."
"6956","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan from Ibrahim ibn Tahman from Matar al-Warraq from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every newborn is pledged for his aqiqa; an animal is slaughtered for him on his seventh day, and he is named, and shaved."
"6957","Narrated Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari from Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi from Muhammad ibn Bakkar from Said ibn Bashir from Matar al-Warraq from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the disbelievers: Kill their aged men, and spare their youths."
"6958","Narrated Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani from al-Haytham ibn Marwan al-Dimashqi from Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd from Said ibn Bashir from Matar al-Warraq from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands when preaching until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"6959","Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar from Rawh ibn Ubada from Ashath from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever prays Subh is under the protection of Allah."
"6960","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Ali ibn al-Madini from Quraysh ibn Anas from Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to cut a strap between his fingers."
"6961","Abu Hurra Wasil ibn Abd al-Rahman from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti from Talq ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan from Hafs ibn Umar al-Najjar from Abu Hurra from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every boy is held in pledge by his aqiqah; it is slaughtered for him on his seventh day, his head is shaved, and he is named."
"6962","Hisham ibn Hassan from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, both said: Narrated Uthman ibn al-Haytham al-Muadhdhin from Hisham ibn Hassan al-Firdawsi from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him."
"6963","Ata ibn Abi Maymuna from al-Hasan. Narrated Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Abu Kamil al-Jahdari from Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymuna, who narrated to me from my father, and Hafs al-Minqari, from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give one salutation facing forward."
"6964","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Raja ibn Muhammad ibn Raja al-Adawi from Shahin Abu Hazim from Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymuna from his father from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is summoned to a ruler and does not answer is a wrongdoer with no right."
"6965","Mujjaa ibn al-Zubayr al-Ataki from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa from Mujjaa ibn Abi Ubayda al-Basri from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling an animal for an animal on credit."
"6966","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa from Mujjaa from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of the house has the greatest right of preemption."
"6967","Humayd al-Tawil from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari from Affan (h), and narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Hudba ibn Khalid, both said: Narrated Hammad ibn Salama from Humayd from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to observe two pauses when he entered the prayer and when he finished the recitation. Imran ibn Husayn disapproved of that, so they wrote about it to Ubayy ibn Kab, and he wrote back to them: Samura spoke the truth."
"6968","Anbasa ibn Abi Raita al-Ghanawi from al-Hasan. Narrated Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani from al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi from Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi from Anbasa al-Awar from al-Hasan from Imran ibn Husayn and Samura ibn Jundub: that a man freed six slaves of his at the time of death, having no wealth besides them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and kept four enslaved."
"6969","Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib from Waki from Yazid ibn Ibrahim from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid mutilation and urge charity."
"6970","Husam ibn Misakk from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Yaqub ibn Malik from Salama ibn Raja from Husam ibn Misakk from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to urge charity and forbid mutilation."
"6971","Ismail ibn Muslim al-Makki from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari from Ismail ibn Muslim al-Makki from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not aim your prayer at sunrise or sunset, for it rises between the two horns of Satan and sets between the two horns of Satan."
"6972","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari from Ismail ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is a portion of the Fire, so cool it from yourselves with cold water. And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had fever, he would call for a skin of water and pour it over his head, then bathe."
"6973","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Asim ibn Ali from Qays ibn al-Rabi from Ismail ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade invoking curses upon one another by the curse of Allah, or by His anger, or by the Fire."
"6974","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Asim ibn Ali from Qays ibn al-Rabi from Ismail ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade one of us to cut a thing or a strap between his fingers."
"6975","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muhammad ibn Abi Nuaym al-Wasiti from Muhammad ibn Yazid from Ismail ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, distance me from my sins as You distanced the east from the west, and purify me from my error as the white garment is purified of filth."
"6976","Narrated Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bakr ibn al-Rabi ibn Muslim from Muhammad ibn Humran from Ismail ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us that when we are three, we put one of us forward as imam, and when we are two, we stand side by side in one row."
"6977","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala from Mutamir ibn Sulayman, who said: I heard Ismail al-Makki narrating from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed for rain, would say: O Allah, send down upon our land its adornment, send down upon our land its tranquility, and provide for us, and You are the best of providers."
"6978","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Tusi from Muhammad ibn Makhlad al-Basri from Muhammad ibn Abi Adi from Ismail ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to join Ramadan with fasting."
"6979","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban from Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman from Ismail ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: We used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when it rained we would hear the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proclaim: Pray in your dwellings."
"6980","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Sahl ibn Uthman from Ali ibn Hashim and al-Muharibi from Ismail ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The boy is held in pledge by his aqiqah; the aqiqah is done for him on the seventh day, he is named, and his head is shaved."
"6981","Narrated Abd Allah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi from Abu Mamar Salih ibn Harb from Sallam ibn Abi Khubza from Ismail ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dozes on Friday while the imam is preaching, let him leave his seat and seat his brother in his place."
"6982","Narrated Abd Allah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi from Abu Mamar Salih ibn Harb from Sallam ibn Abi Khubza from Ismail ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade squatting (iqa) in prayer."
"6983","Mubarak ibn Fadala from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Ibrahim ibn al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Ubulli, who narrated to me from my father, from Mubarak ibn Fadala from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The food of one suffices two, and the food of two suffices four."
"6984","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Ibrahim ibn al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Ubulli, who narrated to me from my father, from Mubarak ibn Fadala from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the hypocrite eats in seven intestines."
"6985","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Sabuni al-Tustari from Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi from Khallad ibn Bazi al-Harrani, master of the litters, from Mubarak ibn Fadala from al-Hasan from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade confining an animal to be shot at, and forbade eating its meat if it was so confined."
"6986","Jarir ibn Hazim from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj from Muhammad ibn Abi Samina from Abu Malik al-Judani from Jarir ibn Hazim from al-Hasan from Samura: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father has consumed my wealth. He said: You and your wealth belong to your father."
"6987","Abu Bakr al-Hudhali from al-Hasan from Samura. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muhammad ibn Abi Nuaym al-Wasiti from Muhammad ibn Yazid from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is that of the tongue. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the charity of the tongue? He said: Intercession by which the captive is freed, blood is spared, good and kindness are drawn to your brother, and harm is repelled from him."
"6988","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan from Fuhayr Yahya ibn Ziyad from Ibn Jurayj from Abu Bakr from al-Hasan from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The food of two suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight."
"6989","Narrated Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil al-Muqri from Ibrahim ibn Salm al-Hujaymi from Awn ibn Umara from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali from al-Hasan from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People never gave any charity like knowledge that is spread."
"6990","Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Ashath from Samura. Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Jawhari from Affan (h), and narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Hudba ibn Khalid, both said: Narrated Hammad ibn Salama (h), and narrated Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi from Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Tawil, narrated Hammad ibn Salama from al-Ashath ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father from Samura ibn Jundub: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw as if a bucket was let down from the sky; Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came and took hold of its handles and drank a weak drink, then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came and took hold of its handles until he was fully satisfied, then Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) came and took hold of its handles and drank until he was fully satisfied, then Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) came and took hold of its handles, but it slipped from him and spilled."
"6991","Hayyaj ibn Imran from Samura ibn Jundub. Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir from Affan from Hammam from Qatada from al-Hasan from Hayyaj ibn Imran from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding mutilation and urging charity."
"6992","Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir Abu al-Ala from Samura ibn Jundub. Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Yahya ibn Main (h), and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, both said: Narrated Yazid ibn Harun, narrated Sulayman al-Taymi from Abu al-Ala ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir from Samura ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bowl of tharid, and it was placed before the people, and they took turns at it from morning until noon, one group rising and another sitting. A man said to Samura: Was it replenished? Samura said: Why do you marvel? It was replenished only from here, and he pointed with his hand toward the sky."
"6993","Abu Ayyub al-Ataki from Samura ibn Jundub. Narrated Abu Zura al-Dimashqi from Muhammad ibn Bakkar from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from Abu Ayyub from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) likened one who comes early on Friday to one who sacrifices a camel, and to one who slaughters a cow, and to one who slaughters a sheep, and to one who slaughters a bird, until he ended at the sparrow."
"6994","Abu Nadra al-Mundhir ibn Malik from Samura. Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza al-Dimashqi from Abu al-Jumahir Muhammad ibn Uthman from Said ibn Bashir from Qatada from Abu Nadra from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the people of the Fire are those whom it seizes up to their ankles, and among them those whom it seizes up to their knees, and among them those whom it seizes up to their waists, and among them those whom it seizes up to their collarbones."
"6995","Narrated Ahmad ibn Anbar al-Basri from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi from Yazid ibn Zuray from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada from Abu Nadra from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among them are those whom the Fire seizes up to their ankles, and among them those whom it seizes up to their waists, and among them those whom it seizes up to their collarbones."
"6996","Al-Asqa ibn al-Asla from Samura. Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sawti from Affan ibn Muslim from Wuhayb ibn Khalid (h), and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim Abu al-Numan from Yazid ibn Zuray from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from Abu Qazaa from al-Asqa ibn al-Asla from Samura ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whatever is below the ankles of the lower garment is in the Fire."
"6997","Abu al-Dahma from Samura ibn Jundub. Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Razi from Ishaq ibn Idris from al-Hasan ibn Dinar from Humayd ibn Hilal from Abu al-Dahma from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will not harm any of you what he staves off hunger with, when he obtains it lawfully."
"6998","Al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufra from Samura ibn Jundub. Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sawti from Affan ibn Muslim from Wahb ibn Khalid (h), and narrated Abd al-Aziz from Abu al-Numan (h), and narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me my father, narrated Muhammad ibn Jafar, narrated Shuba from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufra preaching, saying: Samura ibn Jundub said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not pray when the sun rises, nor when it sets, for it sets between the two horns of Satan and disappears between the two horns of Satan."
"6999","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi from Shuba from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufra narrating from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying after Subh until the sun rises, for it rises upon the two horns of Satan."
"7000","Abu al-Muhallab, uncle of Abu Qilaba al-Jarmi, from Samura ibn Jundub. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from Ayyub from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Muhallab from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adhere to this whiteness; let your living wear it, and shroud your dead in it, for it is among the best of your garments."
"7001","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi from Yazid ibn Zuray from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Ayyub from Abu Qilaba from his uncle Abu al-Muhallab from Samura ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Adhere to whiteness; let your living wear it, and shroud your dead in it, for it is among the best of your garments."
"7002","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Ismail ibn Ulayya from Ayyub from Abu Qilaba from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Adhere to these white garments; let your living wear them, and shroud your dead in them. And Ibn Ulayya did not mention Abu al-Muhallab."
"7003","Abu Mijlaz Lahiq ibn Humayd from Samura ibn Jundub. Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Abu al-Walid from Hammad ibn Salama from Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Mijlaz from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it, the next day at its time."
"7004","Qudama ibn Wabara al-Ujayfi from Samura. Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abd Allah ibn Raja (h), and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Affan ibn Muslim (h), and narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz from Abu Umar al-Hawdi (h), and narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Hudba ibn Khalid (h), and narrated Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi from Ali ibn al-Jad, all said: Narrated Hammam from Qatada from Qudama ibn Wabara from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever misses a Friday without excuse, let him give a dinar in charity; if he does not find one, then half a dinar."
"7005","Sawada ibn Hanzala al-Qushayri from Samura. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, both said: Narrated Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated Hammam, narrated Sawada ibn Hanzala, imam of the mosque of Banu Qushayr, who said: I heard Samura ibn Jundub say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let neither the call of Bilal nor the whiteness seen at the top of dawn deceive you."
"7006","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Amr ibn Marzuq from Shuba from Sawad ibn Hanzala al-Qushayri, who said: I heard Samura ibn Jundub say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let neither the adhan of Bilal nor this darkness deceive you, until it bursts forth like this. And he gestured with his hand horizontally."
"7007","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Hajjaj ibn Nusayr and Abu Umar al-Darir (h), and narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Sulayman ibn Harb (h), and narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani from Hudba ibn Khalid (h), and narrated Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Ziyadi from Muslim ibn Ibrahim, all said: Narrated Abu Hilal from Sawada ibn Hanzala from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let neither the adhan of Bilal nor the elongated dawn prevent you from sahur; rather it is the broad dawn on the horizon. And the wording is that of Hajjaj ibn Nusayr."
"7008","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim Abu al-Numan, and narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to me Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, both said: Narrated Hammad ibn Zayd, narrated Abd Allah ibn Sawada from his father, who said: I heard Samura ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let neither the adhan of Bilal for your sahur nor the whiteness of dawn like this - and he raised his hands - deceive you, until it spreads across the horizon; and he gestured with his hand horizontally."
"7009","Abu Raja al-Utaridi from Samura ibn Jundub. Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib from Hawdha ibn Khalifa from Awf from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, narrated Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among what he would say to his companions: Did any of you see a dream? He said: So we would narrate to him whatever Allah willed that we narrate. He said: Then one morning he said: Last night two men - or two comers - came to me and roused me, and said to me: Go forth. So I went forth with them. We came upon a man lying down, and behold another standing over him with a rock, and he hurls the rock at his head, crushing his head, and the stone rolls away here, so he follows it and takes it, and does not return to him until his head is sound as it was, then he returns to him and does to him as he did the first time. I said to them: Glory be to Allah, what is this? They said to me: Go forth. So we went forth and came upon a man lying on his back, and behold another standing with an iron hook, and he comes to one side of his face and tears his cheek to his nape, then moves to the other side and does the same to it; he does not finish it before that side becomes sound as it was, then he returns to it and does to it as he did the first time. He said: I said to them: Glory be to Allah, who are these two? They said to me: Go forth. So we went forth and came upon a structure like an oven - he said: I think he said - and we heard clamor and voices - he said - so we looked into it, and behold in it naked men and women, and a flame comes to them from beneath them, and when that flame reaches them they cry out. I said to them: Glory be to Allah, who are these? They said to me: Go forth - he said - so we went forth and came upon a river - I thought he said - red like blood, and behold in the river a man swimming, and on the bank of the river a man who had gathered stones beside him, and that swimmer swims as he swims, then comes to the one who gathered stones beside him, and opens his mouth wide for him, so he feeds him a stone; he goes off and swims as he swims, then returns, and every time he returns he opens his mouth wide for him and he feeds him a stone. I said to them: What is this? They said to me: Go forth. So we went forth and came upon a man of hateful appearance, the most hateful-looking man you could see, with a fire which he kindles and circles around - he said - I said to them: What is this? They said to me: Go forth, go forth. So we went forth and came to a lush meadow with every kind of spring greenery, and amid the meadow a tall man whose head I could hardly see for its height in the sky, and around the man the most numerous and most handsome children I had ever seen - he said - I said to them: Glory be to Allah, what is this, and who are these? They said to me: Go forth. So we ended at a great tree, the greatest and finest tree I had ever seen - he said - they said to me: Climb into it. So we climbed, and ended at a city built of bricks of gold and bricks of silver; we came to the gate of the city and sought entry, and it was opened for us, and we entered it, and there met us men half of whose creation was as handsome as you could see, and half as ugly as you could see a man - he said - and they said: Go and fall into that river; and behold a river running across as if its water were pure milk in whiteness - he said - so they went and fell into it, then returned to us with the evil gone from them, become in the finest form - he said - they said to me: This is the Garden of Eden, and that is your dwelling. So my gaze rose upward - he said - and behold a palace like a white cloud - he said - they said: That is your dwelling. I said to them: May Allah bless you, let me go, leave me to enter it. They said to me: As for now, no; but you will enter it - he said - I said to them: I have seen wonders since last night; what is this that I saw? - he said - they said to me: Indeed we shall tell you: As for the first man you came upon whose head is crushed with the stone, he is a man who takes the Quran and sleeps through the obligatory prayer. As for the man you came upon whose cheek, eye and nostril are torn to his nape, he is the man who goes out from his house and tells a lie that reaches the horizons. As for the naked men and women in the structure like an oven, they are the adulterers and adulteresses. As for the man swimming in the river and being fed stones, he is the devourer of usury. As for the hateful-looking man beside him, he is Malik, keeper of Hell. As for the man in the meadow, he is Ibrahim (peace be upon him), and as for the children around him, every newborn upon the fitra. He said: And some of the Muslims said: O Messenger of Allah, and the children of the polytheists? He said: And the children of the polytheists. And as for the people half of whom were handsome and half ugly, they are a people who mixed a righteous deed with another evil one, so Allah overlooked them."
"7010","Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki, in Egypt, from Muawiya ibn Ata al-Khuzai from Shuba from Awf from Abu Raja al-Utaridi from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), every morning, would say to his companions: Did any of you see a dream? He said: And one day he awoke and said: I saw as if two men came to me and said: Go forth, go forth. So I went forth with them until they brought me to a white-haired, white-bearded old man, gloomy and sorrowful, beside a fire which he kindles and tends. I said: May Allah bless you, who is this old man, and what is this fire? They said to me: Go forth, go forth. So I went forth with them until they brought me to a man, and behold a man standing over his head with an iron hook in his hand, tearing his mouth to his nape, his nostril to his nape, and his eye to his nape, then doing the same to the other side; he does not finish it before that side returns as sound as it was. I said: O may Allah bless you, who are these two men? They said to me: Go forth, go forth. So I went forth with them until they brought me to a man lying on his back, and behold a man standing over his head with a rock in his hand, crushing his head with it, and the stone rolls to a place far away, so he goes and takes it, and does not return to his companion before his head returns as sound as it was, and he does to him as before. I said: O may Allah bless you, who are these two? They said: Go forth, go forth. So I went forth with them until they brought me to something like a pond, and in it a man swimming, and a man standing on the edge of the pond with a rock in his hand; the swimmer comes and opens his mouth wide for him, so he feeds him that stone. I said: O may Allah bless you, who are these two? They said to me: Go forth, go forth. So I went forth with them until they brought me to something like an oven, and in it men and women, and a flame comes to them from below, and they cry out. I said: O may Allah bless you, who are these? They said to me: Go forth, go forth. So I went forth with them until they brought me to a white land as if of silver, with every blossom of spring in it, and a white-haired, white-bearded man, as handsome as you could see, with children beside him whom he gathers and tends. I said: O may Allah bless you, who is this old man, and who are these children? They said to me: Go forth, go forth. So I went forth with them until they brought me to a white land as if of silver, with a river flowing in it; and there come a people half of whose bodies are as handsome as you could see, and half as ugly as you could see; they enter that river as if commanded, and come out as if anointed with oil. I said: O may Allah bless you, who are these? They said: Go forth, go forth. So I went forth with them until they brought me to the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, which is the Garden of Eden, and that is your dwelling. I said: O may Allah bless you, let me enter it. They said: No; but you will enter it. I said: O may Allah bless you, I have seen wonders since last night. They said: We shall tell you: As for the one you saw white-haired and white-bearded, that is Malik, keeper of Hell. As for the one you saw whose mouth is torn to his nape and his nostril to his nape, that is a man who leaves his house telling a lie that spreads through the horizons. As for the one you saw whose head is crushed, left as if a loaf, that is the talebearer. As for the one you saw in the pond being fed a stone, that is the man who devours the orphan's wealth. As for the one you saw in what resembles an oven, they are the adulteresses and adulterers. As for the white-haired, white-bearded one you saw, that is Ibrahim, friend of Allah, and the children you saw are the children of the Muslims, and every newborn is born upon the fitra. As for those you saw half of whose bodies were as handsome as you could see and half as ugly as you could see, they are a people who did a righteous deed and another evil one, so Allah forgives them."
"7011","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi from Harun ibn al-Mughira from Anbasa ibn Said from Abu Hashim al-Wasiti from Abu al-Harith al-Abdi from Abu Raja al-Utaridi from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he awoke, would say: Did any of you see a dream? And he would interpret it for him, until one day he awoke and said: Did any of you see a dream? The people fell silent, so he said: But I saw in a dream: two men came to me and said to me: Go forth. They passed me by a man with a rock in his hand, striking therewith the head of a man, scattering his brains; the rock returns to his hand and his head returns as it was - he said - I said: What is this? They said: Go forth. They passed me by a man with an iron hook in his hand, tearing therewith the cheek of a man, until when it reached its end he took to the other, and this one returned as it was. I said: What is this? They said to me: Go forth. They passed me by a man in a river of blood, bridled, with a man on the bank of the river kindling a fire with stones in it; every time he wished to come out, he took a stone from it and cast it into his mouth, so he returned. I said: What is this? They said to me: Go forth. They passed me by a house whose bottom is narrower than its top, with naked people in it, and fire kindled beneath them; whenever it is kindled they clamor, and when it is extinguished they grow still. I said: What is this? They said to me: Go forth. They passed me by a tree, beneath which a man kindles a fire and tends it; when it scatters he gathers it. I said: What is this? They said to me: Go forth, until they brought me to the middle of a tree, with handsome dwellings. I said: What is this? They said to me: Go forth. They took me to the top of the tree, with dwellings finer than them, and three chambers. I said: What is this? They said: Wait: as for the one with a rock in his hand striking the head of the man, they are those who sleep through prayer - and Ibn Abbas said: this is one given knowledge who is awakened for it - and as for the man you saw with an iron hook tearing therewith the cheek of a man, they are those who carry tales. As for the one you saw in a river of blood, they are the devourers of usury. As for those you saw in the narrow-bottomed house with naked people, they are the adulterers of the umma, and so they shall be until the Day of Resurrection. As for the man you saw beneath the tree kindling the fire and tending it, he is Malik, keeper of the Fire. As for the dwellings you saw in the middle of the tree, they are the dwellings of the believers in general; and these are the dwellings of the prophets, the truthful and the martyrs; and this chamber is yours. And I am Jibril, and this is Mikail."
"7012","Narrated Yaqub ibn Ghaylan al-Umani from Abu Kurayb from Yunus ibn Bukayr from Khalid ibn Dinar al-Basri, narrated to me Abu Raja al-Utaridi, narrated Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque one day and said: Which of you saw a dream, let him narrate it. Then he mentioned something similar."
"7013","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami from Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim from my father, narrated Abu Raja al-Utaridi from Samura ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Which of you saw a dream? Then he mentioned something similar."
"7014","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl from Musa ibn Ismail from Jarir ibn Hazim from Abu Raja from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise."
"7015","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Missisi from Dawud ibn Mansur al-Qadi from Jarir ibn Hazim from Abu Raja al-Utaridi from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came one day - and when he prayed he would turn to us with his face - and said: Did any of you see a dream last night? If any of us had seen a dream he would narrate it to him, and he would say concerning it whatever Allah willed. One day he asked us: Did any of you see a dream? We said: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw two men come to me; they took my hands and brought me out to a level land - or an open space. I passed by a man with another standing over his head, with an iron hook in his hand which he inserts into this cheek of his, tearing it until it reaches his nape, then doing the same to his other cheek, while this cheek of his heals, so he returns and does the same to it. I said: What is this? They said: Go forth. So we went forth until we came upon a man lying on his back, with a man standing over his head with a rock - or a millstone - crushing his head therewith; the stone rolls away, so he goes to take it, and does not return to this one before his head heals, his head restored as it was, so he returns to him and strikes him; he keeps doing that to him. I said: What is this? They said: Go forth. So we went forth until we ended at a house built like an oven, its top narrow and its bottom wide, with fire kindled beneath it, and in it naked men and women; when it is kindled beneath them they rise until they almost come out of it, and when it subsides they return into it. I said: What is this? They said: Go forth. So we went forth until we came upon a river of blood with a man standing in the middle of the river, and a man before him with stones; he throws at the man in the river, and whenever he wishes to come out of it, the man throws a stone into his mouth, returning him to where he was. I said: What is this? They said: Go forth. So we went forth until we ended at a red meadow with a great tree, at whose root an old man with boys and women around him, and a man at the tree with a fire before him which he kindles and tends. I asked them both, and they said: Go forth. So we went forth until we came to the tree, and they admitted me into a house the like of which in beauty I had never seen, with old men, youths, boys and women in it. Then they took me up the tree and admitted me into another house, finer and better than the first, with old men and youths in it. I said to them: You have taken me around since last night, and pitied me, so tell me about what I saw. They said: Yes. As for the first man you saw, he is a liar who would tell a lie carried from him until it reaches the horizons, so there shall be done to him what you saw until the Day of Resurrection. As for the man whose head is crushed, that is a man whom Allah taught the Quran, but he slept through it by night and did not act upon it by day, so there shall be done to him what you saw until the Day of Resurrection. As for those you saw in the house, they are the adulterers of this umma. As for the one you saw in the river of blood, he is the devourer of usury. As for the old man you saw at the root of the tree, that is Ibrahim (peace be upon him); as for the boys you saw, they are the children of the people. As for the fire you saw and the man kindling it, that is the Fire, and that is the keeper of the Fire. As for the first house you entered, it is the house of Aisha, Mother of the Believers; and as for this one, it is the house of the martyrs. And I am Jibril, and this is Mikail. I said to them: Tell me, where is my dwelling? They said: Raise your head. So I raised my head, and behold above me as if a cloud. They said: That is your dwelling. I said: Let me enter my dwelling. They said: You still have deeds you have not yet completed; when you complete them, you will enter your dwelling."
"7016","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi from Hisham ibn Ammar from al-Rabi ibn Badr from Awf from Abu Raja from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best remedy people treat themselves with is cupping."
"7017","Narrated Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi from Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi from Jafar ibn Sulayman from Awf from Abu Raja al-Utaridi from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is but like a rib; if you straighten her you will break her, so deal gently with her and you will live with her."
"7018","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Uqba ibn Mukram al-Dabbi from Isa ibn Shuayb from Abbad ibn Mansur from Abu Raja from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the children of the polytheists, and he said: They are the servants of the people of Paradise."
"7019","Muhammad ibn Sirin from Samura. Narrated Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri from Rayhan Abu Ghassan from al-Salt ibn Muhammad Abu Hammam al-Kharaki from Awf ibn Mamar al-Udi from Ibrahim al-Saigh, who said: I asked Matar al-Warraq: Does a man recite In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, and seek refuge from Satan the accursed in every raka and in every sura he begins? He said: Qatada narrated to me from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Imran ibn Husayn and Samura ibn Jundub, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: They are the two pauses; he does that silently when he opens the prayer and when he rises from sitting in the two rakas."
"7020","Sulayman ibn Samura from his father. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym from Musa ibn Muhammad al-Ansari from Abu Malik al-Ashjai from Nuaym ibn Abi Hind from Ibn Samura ibn Jundub from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever kills a slain one, his spoils belong to him."
"7021","Narrated Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamza al-Zubayri, narrated to me my father (h), and narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated Ibrahim ibn Hamza al-Zubayri (h), and narrated Ali ibn Said, narrated Abu Musab, narrated Hatim ibn Ismail from Ibn Jurayj from Abu Malik al-Ashjai from Said ibn Tariq from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a slain one, his spoils belong to him."
"7022","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura, narrated to me Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Whoever kills a slain one, his spoils belong to him."
"7023","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura, narrated Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: Whoever kills a man, his spoils from the fay belong to him when he picks it up."
"7024","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani (h), and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, both said: Narrated Marwan ibn Muawiya from Abu Malik al-Ashjai from Nuaym ibn Abi Hind from a son of Samura from Samura, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a rainy day - I think he said: on a journey - his caller would proclaim: Pray in your dwellings."
"7025","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Missisi from Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba from Abu Ishaq al-Fazari from Abu Malik al-Ashjai from Nuaym ibn Abi Hind, who said: Samura ibn Jundub said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a slain one, his spoils belong to him."
"7026","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Musa ibn Harun, both said: Narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: To proceed: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us that each of us pray every night after the obligatory prayer, little or much, and make it witr."
"7027","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura, narrated to me Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father Sulayman from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us that a man pray every night after the obligatory prayer, much or little, and make it witr."
"7028","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Musa ibn Harun, both said: Narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dozes during Friday, let him move from his seat."
"7029","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura, narrated to me Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us: When one of you dozes during Friday, let him move from his seat to another place."
"7030","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Musa ibn Harun, both said: Narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"7031","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Musa ibn Harun, both said: Narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: If one of you had a valley full from its top to its bottom, he would love to have another valley filled for him. He said: By Allah, if I could I would fill you; and a man's soul is never filled with wealth until it is filled with dust."
"7032","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa, narrated Jafar ibn Sulayman ibn Sad ibn Samura, narrated to me Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father Sulayman from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to pray at whatever hour we wished of the night or day, except that he commanded us to avoid sunrise and sunset, and said: Satan disappears with it and rises with it when it rises."
"7033","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura ibn Jundub from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb from his father from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to pray at whatever hour we wished of the night or day, except that he commanded us to avoid sunrise and sunset, and said: Satan disappears with it when it sets, and rises with it when it rises."
"7034","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura, narrated to me Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father Sulayman from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to guard all the prayers, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined the middle prayer, and told us that it is the Asr prayer."
"7035","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to guard all the prayers, enjoined the middle prayer, and told us that it is the Asr prayer."
"7036","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura, narrated to me Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father Sulayman from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to fast continuously in the month of fasting, disliking it, though not as a firm prohibition."
"7037","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to fast continuously in the month of fasting, disliking it, though not as a firm command."
"7038","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura, narrated Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father Sulayman from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us not to curse with the curse of Allah and His anger."
"7039","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cursing one another by the curse of Allah or by His anger, and forbade us to curse one another by the Fire."
"7040","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us that when prayer overtakes us and we are three or more, one of us should stand forth as our imam; and if we are two, we should stand together."
"7041","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura, narrated to me Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father Sulayman from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us that when prayer overtakes us and we are three or more, we put forward one of us as imam; and if we are two, we stand together entirely."
"7042","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to love one another, and to greet one another when we meet."
"7043","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura, narrated to me Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father Sulayman from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us that when we are in the middle of prayer, or at the time of its ending, begin before the salutation by saying: Greetings, good words, prayers, peace and sovereignty belong to Allah; then send peace upon the prophets, then send peace upon your kin and upon yourselves."
"7044","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, narrated Jafar ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is time for the salutation in the middle of prayer, or at its ending, begin before the salutation by saying: Greetings, good words, prayers, peace and sovereignty belong to Allah; then send peace upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then send peace upon your kin and upon yourselves."
"7045","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa al-Kufi, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura, narrated to me Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father Sulayman from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us that when we are in prayer and raise our heads from prostration, we settle upon the ground sitting, and not spring up upon the edges of the feet."
"7046","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa, narrated Jafar ibn Sad, narrated Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid a man to remain celibate, and declared forbidden entering the houses of the believers uninvited."
"7047","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman, narrated Jafar ibn Sad from Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid a man to remain celibate, and declare forbidden entering the houses of the believers."
"7048","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura, narrated to me Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father Sulayman from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Whoever conceals one who misappropriates spoils is like him; and whoever joins a polytheist and dwells with him is like him."
"7049","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever conceals one who misappropriates spoils is like him; and whoever gathers with a polytheist and dwells with him is like him."
"7050","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura ibn Khubayb, who said: When two men of us traded with each other, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have one of them sell with the option until he parts from his companion, each of them giving the other choice, so each chooses his desire in the bargain."
"7051","Narrated Abdan, narrated Duhaym, narrated Yahya ibn Hassan, narrated Sulayman ibn Musa, narrated Jafar ibn Sad, narrated to me Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command that mosques be built in our quarters, that their construction be kept good and that they be purified."
"7052","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, narrated Jafar ibn Sad from Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to build the mosque in our quarters, to make its construction good and to purify it."
"7053","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman, narrated Jafar ibn Sad, narrated Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father from Samura, who said: There came to him - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - a Bedouin man asking him about a man: what is lawful for him and what is forbidden to him in his wealth, his rites, his livestock, his atira and his fara of the offspring of his camels and his barren ones? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I permit for you the good things and forbid for you the foul things, except that you become needy of food, then you may eat of it until you are free of need of it. And the man asked him then: What is my poverty at which I may eat that, or my sufficiency that frees me of it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you expect offspring, so you sustain your livestock's meat until your offspring, or you expect rain to fall within reach, so you sustain yourself therewith by your livestock's meat, or you expect a provision of wealth, so you reach it by your livestock's meat; and when you expect nothing of that, then feed your family as it seems to you until you are free of need of it. The Bedouin said: And what is my sufficiency which I leave when I find it? He said: When you have watered your family with the evening milk, then avoid what is forbidden to you of food. As for your wealth, it is all easy for you, none of it forbidden, except that in your offspring of your camels is a fara, and in your offspring of your sheep is a fara, which your livestock nourish until it is grown; then if you wish feed it to your family, and if you wish give its meat in charity. And he commanded him to offer an atira of sheep, ten of every hundred."
"7054","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa, narrated Jafar ibn Sad, narrated to me Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us concerning a man's or woman's slave who is his inherited property, engaged in his work, whom he does not wish to sell: he used to command us not to pay any charity on their account, and he used to command us to pay charity on that which is prepared for sale."
"7055","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to revile, and said: If one of you must revile his companion, let him not slander him, nor revile his parents, nor revile his people; but if he knows that, let him say: You are miserly, or let him say: You are cowardly, or let him say: You are a liar, or let him say: You are ignoble."
"7056","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: Do not swear by the taghuts, nor swear by your fathers; swear by Allah, for He loves that you swear by Him, and do not swear by anything besides Him."
"7057","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb from Jafar ibn Sad from Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father from Samura (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to recite the Noble Quran as we were taught it, and said: It was sent down in three modes; do not differ over it, nor dispute over it, for it is blessed, so recite it as you were taught it."
"7058","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Arabs are the children of Sam ibn Nuh, the Romans are the children of Yafith ibn Nuh, and the Abyssinians are the children of Ham ibn Nuh."
"7059","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us that if one of us was distracted from prayer or forgot it until its time passed, we should pray it along with the next obligatory prayer."
"7060","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, narrated Jafar ibn Sad from Khubayb ibn Sulayman from his father from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The month does not complete thirty nights. Musa ibn Harun said: Its meaning is that not every month completes thirty, i.e. sometimes it is twenty-nine."
"7061","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, narrated Jafar ibn Sad from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you stand for prayer, do not precede your reciter in bowing, prostration and standing; rather let him precede you, and you will make up what you were preceded in thereby, when he raises his head in bowing, prostration and standing before you, so you attain what you missed thereby."
"7062","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: When you fight the polytheists, kill their elders, for the softest-hearted among them are their youths."
"7063","And with his chain from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you spits while in prayer, let him not spit in front of his face nor to his right, but spit beneath his foot and rub it into the ground."
"7064","And with his chain from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us that whoever loses property or it is stolen, then recognizes it, and a year passes over it, his property shall be returned to him; and the one who bought it shall sell its price back to the seller from whom he bought."
"7065","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - in the year of the Conquest -: This is the year of the Greater Hajj. He said: The hajj of the Muslims and the hajj of the polytheists coincided in three consecutive days, and the hajj of the Muslims, the polytheists, the Christians and the Jews coincided this year in six consecutive days; and they had not so coincided since the heavens and earth were created before this year, nor shall they coincide after this year until the Hour comes."
"7066","And with his chain from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid women to lie down together except with garments between them, and that a man lie down with his companion except with a garment between them."
"7067","With his chain from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbids a Muslim to draw a weapon against a Muslim."
"7068","And with his chain from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"7069","And with his chain from Samura: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Whoever of you prepares food enough for two men, it will suffice three; or prepares for three, it will suffice four; or for four, it will suffice five - and so on in number."
"7070","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to attend Friday and not to absent ourselves from it; and when the believers are called to a call on Friday and rise, each of them has the greatest right to his seat when he returns to it."
"7071","And with his chain from Samura, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that there came to him a Bedouin man asking him about what is forbidden to him and what is lawful for him, and about his rites and his livestock, and about his atira and his fara of the offspring of his camels and sheep? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: The good things are lawful for you, and the foul things are forbidden to you, except that you become needy of food unlawful to you, then you may eat of it until you are free of need of it. And a man asked him then: What is my poverty, and what may I eat thereof when I reach it, and what is my sufficiency that frees me of it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: When you expect offspring, so you sustain yourself by your livestock's meat until your offspring, or you expect rain you think will reach you, so you sustain yourself by your livestock's meat, or you expect a provision you will obtain, so you reach it by your livestock's meat; and if you expect nothing of that, then feed your family as it seems to you until you are free of need of it. The Bedouin said: What is my sufficiency which I leave when I find it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: When you have watered your family with the evening milk, then avoid what is forbidden to you of food. As for your wealth, it is all easy for you, with nothing forbidden in it, except that in your offspring of your camels is a fara, and in your offspring of your sheep is a fara, which your livestock nourish until it is grown; then if you wish feed it to your family, and if you wish give its meat in charity. And he commanded him to offer an atira of sheep, an atira from every grazing flock."
"7072","And with his chain from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command concerning a man's or woman's slave who are his inherited property and his laborers, whom he does not wish to sell: he used to command us not to pay any charity on their account, and he used to command us to pay charity on slaves prepared for sale."
"7073","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: When one of you prays, let him say: O Allah, distance between me and my sin as You distanced between the east and the west; O Allah, I seek refuge in You lest You turn Your face from me on the Day of Resurrection; O Allah, purify me of my sin as the white garment is purified of filth; O Allah, keep me alive as a Muslim and cause me to die as a Muslim."
"7074","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us one day: It was said to me: Recite to Ibn al-Khattab. So he summoned him and commanded that the Quran be present when it is sent down, to recite it to him."
"7075","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid plunder, so much so that he would command the company about the sheep's meat while they were cooking it, saying: Do not eat it."
"7076","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: A woman is but like a rib; if you try to straighten her you will break her, or you leave her while she is crooked."
"7077","And with his chain from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The prophets on the Day of Resurrection, every two of them will be close friends apart from the rest. He said: So my close friend among them that day will be Ibrahim, friend of Allah (peace be upon him)."
"7078","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prophets vie as to which of them has more companions from his umma, so I hope that day to be the greatest of them all in arrivals. For every man of them that day stands at a full pond with a staff, calling whom he knows of his umma, and every umma has a mark by which its prophet knows them."
"7079","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the nations is a nation struck for them a parable like hirelings whom a man hires to work for him the whole day, appointing for them a qirat. They worked until midday, grew weary, and said to the man: Settle with us. So he settled with them, and they received half a qirat. He said: Who will complete my work until night for a qirat each? So another people contracted with him and worked until near the Asr prayer, grew weary, and said: Settle with us. So he settled with them, and they received half a qirat. And the man wished his work completed before night, so he hired a people to complete what remained of his work until night for two qirats. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: I hope, if Allah wills, that you are the people of the two qirats."
"7080","And with his chain from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man of the Ansar came to him asking him about kalala: Tell me, O Messenger of Allah, is the kalala of a man meaning brothers from his mother and father? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said nothing to him except that he recited to him the verse of kalala in Surat al-Nisa. Then the man returned asking him, and whenever he asked him he recited it, until he asked much and the man raised his voice, his clamor intensifying out of eagerness for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to clarify for him. So he recited the verse to him, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: By Allah, I shall not add for you beyond what you were given, by Allah, I shall not add for you beyond what you were given, until he added against him. Then the man sat down and fell silent."
"7081","And with his chain from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid the owner of palm trees to incur debt against the fruit of his palms until its fruit is eaten, fearing he incur a large debt while the fruit spoils and does not cover him; and he used to forbid the owner of crops to incur debt against his crop until harvest time; and he used to forbid the owner of gold, when he sells it for food of the fruit, to sell the food for gold until the food is measured and taken possession of, fearing usury."
"7082","And with his chain from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: Abu Bakr interpreted the dream, and the righteous dream is a share of prophethood."
"7083","And with his chain from Samura, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the polytheists in prayer, he would begin with Quraysh, then follow them with many tribes of the Arabs. Once it was said to him: Curse the disbelievers of Quraysh. So when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wished to curse a tribe, he would say: O Allah, curse the disbelievers of Quraysh, the sons of so-and-so."
"7084","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: It is not lawful for a Muslim man to mutilate his slave nor to castrate him; and whomever we know did any of that, we shall do the same to him."
"7085","And with his chain from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: No road is cut off, nor is surplus water withheld; and for the wayfarer is the loan of the bucket, the rope and the trough, if he has not rendered it in kind; and he is left with the well to water, and the digger is not prevented, when the digger descends twenty-five cubits, a resting place for livestock."
"7086","Narrated Musa ibn Harun, narrated Marwan ibn Jafar, narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura, narrated Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to honor the guest."
"7087","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid milking a man's livestock without his permission, and say: Their milk is but as what is in your enclosures; neither is more lawful than the other."
"7088","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The sun and the moon are not eclipsed for the death of any of you, nor for anything you innovate; rather that is among the signs of Allah by which He moves His servants, so that whoever fears Him gives thanks and remembers Him. When you see some of the signs of Allah, Almighty and Exalted, hasten to the remembrance of Allah; remember Him and fear Him. And he prayed for us on the day the sun eclipsed, then admonished and reminded us, then said: Nothing you saw of anything in this world having color, nor were you told of in Paradise or in the Fire, but was pictured for me in front of this wall since I prayed this prayer of mine for you; I looked at it distinctly in the wall of the mosque."
"7089","And with his chain from Samura, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: There is no envy in this world except in two: a man envies a man whom Allah gives much wealth, so he spends of it abundantly; the other says: Had I the like of this, I would spend as he spends and better; so he envies him. And a man recites the Quran and stands with it by night, with another man beside him who does not know the Quran, so he envies him for his standing and for what Allah, Almighty and Exalted, taught him of the Quran, saying: Had Allah taught me the like of this, I would stand as he stands."
"7090","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: Do not meet the caravans before they reach their market."
"7091","And with his chain from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Do not sell to the Bedouins, even if he be the brother, father or mother of one of you."
"7092","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Whoever sells land or a house, the neighbor of the land and the neighbor of the house has the greatest right to buy it when he offers its price."
"7093","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: When a woman is married and two different men marry her, both guardians, the worthier of the two marriers is the first of them; and in a sale, when two men buy one commodity, the worthier of them is the first of them."
"7094","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid shighar with women."
"7095","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid three that two of them converse privately to the exclusion of the other."
"7096","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us when we raided: if a man calls at the rear of the people, saying: O first one, that he wait for him until he catches up."
"7097","And with his chain from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid that when a man is invited to food, he bring someone with him, unless the hosts permit him."
"7098","And with his chain from Samura: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came to him asking about eating lizard, and he said: I neither command it nor forbid anyone from it, except that we, the family of Muhammad, do not eat it."
"7099","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us once at night, while we were encamped at a pit, to eat the meat of the domestic donkey; and he commanded us concerning meat with us, so we cast it away."
"7100","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: By Allah, it would not delight me to have Uhud all in gold and then bequeath it."
"7101","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: Each of you on the day he dies has three friends: among them one who withholds from him what he asks, and that is his wealth; and among them a friend who goes with him until he enters the grave, giving him nothing and accompanying him no further, and those are his kin; and among them a friend who says: By Allah, I go with you wherever you go, and shall never part from you; and that is his deed, whether good or evil."
"7102","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: You shall be gathered to Bayt al-Maqdis, then assembled on the Day of Resurrection."
"7103","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid one of us to notch a strap between his fingers, saying: In that are two eyes."
"7104","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: When a man disputes with another, and one of them calls his fellow to the Messenger to judge between them, whoever refuses to come has no right."
"7105","And with his chain from Samura, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek forgiveness for the believing men and women, and the Muslim men and women, every Friday."
"7106","And with his chain from Samura, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when it rained while we were traveling and the call to prayer was made, out of dislike of burdening us, would order the muadh-dhin to say: Pray in your lodgings."
"7107","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: I become angry with you and I excuse you, then I supplicate Allah privately between me and Him: O Allah, whatever of them I have cursed, or reviled, or become angry with, make it for them a blessing, mercy, forgiveness and prayer, for they are my family and I am sincere toward them."
"7108","And with his chain from Samura, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The False Messiah, the Dajjal, is blind in his left eye, over it is a thick membrane, and he will cure the one blind from birth and the leper, and give life to the dead, and he will say: I am your lord; so whoever holds fast to Allah and says: My Lord is Allah, then refuses that, until he dies, there is no punishment upon him nor trial; and whoever says: You are my lord, he has been put to trial. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The False Messiah, the Dajjal, will remain on earth as long as Allah wills, then Isa ibn Maryam (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will come from the east, affirming Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and following his religion, then he will kill the False Messiah, the Dajjal."
"7109","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour is established you will see grave things that you will deem abominable, and you will say: We are doomed; we were told of this; so when you see that, remember Allah Almighty, and know that they are the beginnings of the Hour. Until he said: You will see mountains move from their places before the Blast truly comes to pass. And he used to say to us: The Hour will not be established until a stone points to a Jew hiding; a Muslim man pursues him, he appears before him, then hides, and the stone says: O servant of Allah, this is what you seek."
"7110","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: There is no regret in this world except in three cases: a man who had crops to irrigate, and he had a water-drawing camel with which he irrigated his land, and when his land became intensely thirsty and its fruits emerged, his water-camel died, so he feels regret for his water-camel which he had trained to draw water, at not finding its like, and he feels regret for the fruit of his land lest it spoil before he can find a means for it; and a man who had a fine swift horse, and he met a gathering of disbelievers, and when they drew near one another the enemies of Allah fled, and the man outstripped them on his horse, and when he was about to catch up his horse broke down with him, and he was left standing beside it, feeling regret for his horse at not finding its like, and feeling regret for the victory he missed which he had been on the verge of; and a man with a wife whose appearance and religion pleased him, and she gave birth to a boy in childbed, then died in childbirth, so he feels regret for his wife thinking he will never meet her like, and he feels regret for her child fearing it will perish from neglect before he finds a wet-nurse for it. He said: And this is the greatest of those regrets."
"7111","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command the Muhajirun and the Ansar to be in the front rows, and he would say: They know prayer better than the bedouins and the foolish, and those behind them follow them in prayer, and I do not like the bedouins to be in front of them, for they do not know how prayer is."
"7112","And with his chain from Samura, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a tree standing apart on a single trunk, the width of its trunk is a seventy-year journey."
"7113","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: The name of the believing man in the Books is al-karm (the noble vine), because Allah honored him above creation; and you call a wall of grapes al-karm, but its name is al-hafr (the dug trench), and the man, he is al-karm."
"7114","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Al-Firdaws is the hill of Paradise, its middle part, which is its highest and best."
"7115","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: I do not find any species of beasts in which a single beast is better than a hundred of its fellows, except man: you find a man who is better than a hundred men."
"7116","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Whoever holds land as a pledge for a debt owed by him, he repays from its fruit what remains after its expenses, and he repays that toward what he owes from the time of it, after reckoning for its holder - the one with whom it is - his labor and his expenses justly."
"7117","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us, on the day he came to Hijr of Thamud, at a well beside al-Madina, from drinking from it or giving water from it, and he forbade us from entering their houses; and he informed us that the she-camel's calf climbed a small mountain - I heard people call it Kinana - and that the trace of the she-camel's calf is clearly visible on its front."
"7118","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided or traveled, then came back returning to al-Madina, he would say: Returning, praising our Lord, worshipping our Lord."
"7119","Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Marwan ibn Jafar al-Simmari from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Khubayb ibn Samura from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura ibn Jundub, that a man once said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When the Confederates come, forbid the people of al-Madina from watering the date-palms; so he said: If I were to forbid you, you would be scorched, and the forbidding of the Prophets, the mountains cannot bear it."
"7120","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of excess and arrogance, for many of the Children of Israel went to excess, until a short woman would make two clogs of wood and stuff them, then insert her feet into them, then go to a tall woman and walk with her, until she equaled her or became taller than her."
"7121","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when he sought rain: O Allah, send down in our land its adornment; O Allah, send down in our land its tranquility."
"7122","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Banu Ghifar and Aslam were, like many people, a trial; they say: Had it been good, Allah would not have made them the first of people in it; yet Ghifar - may Allah forgive it - and Aslam - may Allah grant it peace."
"7123","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan - Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to me - from Jafar ibn Sad - Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura narrated to me - from his father from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: One of you will soon wish to see me a single glance, in exchange for what he has of family and wealth."
"7124","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura - Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura narrated to me - from his father from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: You will soon be among people like salt in food; food is not good except with salt."
"7125","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa from Jafar ibn Sad - Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura narrated to me - from his father from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you seize his companion's captive unrightfully; when he has taken him, he kills him."
"7126","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa from Jafar ibn Sad - Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura narrated to me - from his father from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: There is not a man among you but I am holding his waist-wrap lest he fall into the Fire."
"7127","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa from Jafar ibn Sad from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: Whoever among you is killed, patient and advancing, killed in the path of Allah, is in Paradise."
"7128","Narrated Abdan from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa from Jafar ibn Sad from Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura from his father from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the battle-cry of the Muhajirun: O Banu Abd al-Rahman, and the battle-cry of the Khazraj: O Banu Abd Allah, and the battle-cry of the Aws: O Banu Ubayd Allah, and he named our horses: the horses of Allah, when we took fright."
"7129","And with his chain from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: When we took fright, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would command unity, patience and calm, and when we fought."
"7130","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura - Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura narrated to me - from his father from Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: My nation is a nation that will enter Paradise; among them are seventy thousand without reckoning."
"7131","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Duhaym from Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Musa from Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura - Khubayb ibn Sulayman narrated to me - from his father from Samura ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: I enter this chamber, and I do not enter it at that time except fearing that there may be wealth in it, and I die without having spent it."
"7132","Samura Abu Jabir al-Suwai. Narrated Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Asbahani from Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni from Ismail ibn Ubayd Allah from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhab from Jabir ibn Samura from his father Samura al-Suwai, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We are people of the desert and livestock; should we perform ablution from camel meat and its milk? He said: Yes. I said: Should we perform ablution from sheep meat and its milk? He said: No."
"7133","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Musa ibn Ismail from Jarir ibn Hazim, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Yaqub narrating from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us during one of the two daytime prayers - Zhuhr or Asr - carrying al-Hasan or al-Husayn; he stepped forward and placed him at his right foot, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated a prostration and lengthened it; so I raised my head from among the people, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating, and the boy riding his back; so I returned and prostrated; then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, some people said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), you prostrated in this prayer of yours a prostration you never used to prostrate; were you commanded something, or was revelation sent to you? He said: Neither happened, but my son rode me, and I disliked to hurry him until he finished his need."
"7134","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ibn Jurayj - Ikrima ibn Khalid informed me - from Abu Ammar from Shaddad ibn al-Had, that a bedouin man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), believed in him and followed him, and said: I will emigrate with you; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted him to his Companions; then when the battle of Khaybar - or he said: Hunayn - took place, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gained some spoils, divided them, and allotted him a share, and gave his Companions what he had allotted him, while he was pasturing their riding animals; when he came they handed it to him, and he said: What is this? They said: A share the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted for you; so he took it and brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Muhammad, what is this? He said: A share I allotted for you. He said: I did not follow you for this, but I followed you that I be shot here - and he pointed to his throat - with an arrow, then die and enter Paradise; so he said: If you are truthful to Allah, He will be truthful to you; they stayed a little, then rose to fight the enemy, and he was brought carried, struck by an arrow where he had pointed; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is it he, he? He said: Yes. He said: He was truthful to Allah, so He was truthful to him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded him in the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cloak, then brought him forward and prayed over him; and among what appeared of his prayer over him was: O Allah, this is Your servant who went out emigrating in Your path, and was killed a martyr; I am a witness over him."
"7135","Shaddad ibn Usayd al-Sulami. Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Ali ibn al-Madini, and narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar from Abda ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar, both saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us from Amr ibn Qayzi ibn Amir ibn Shaddad ibn Usayd al-Sulami al-Madani - my father narrated to me - from his grandfather Shaddad, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged to him upon emigration, then fell ill, and he said: What is wrong with you, O Shaddad? He said: I said: I fell ill, O Messenger of Allah, and had I drunk from the water of Batha I would have recovered; he said: What prevents you? I said: My emigration. He said: Then go, for you are an emigrant wherever you are."
"7136","Shaddad Abu al-Mustawrid al-Fihri, and he is Shaddad ibn Amr ibn Hasal ibn al-Ajabb ibn Amr ibn Shayban ibn Muharib ibn Fihr ibn Malik. Narrated al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda al-Antaki and Nuaym ibn Muhammad al-Turi, both saying: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us from al-Walid ibn Muslim from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I took his hand, and it was softer than silk and cooler than snow."
"7137","Shaddad ibn Shurahbil al-Ansari. Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza al-Dimashqi and Khayr ibn Arafa al-Misri, both saying: Haywa ibn Shurayh al-Himsi narrated to us from Baqiyya ibn al-Walid from Habib ibn Salih from Ayyash ibn Munis from Shaddad ibn Shurahbil al-Ansari, who said: Whatever I may forget, I have not forgotten that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing praying, with his right hand over his left, grasping it."
"7138","Shaddad ibn Aws al-Ansari, kunya Abu Abd al-Rahman, and he is the sister's son of Hassan ibn Thabit; he settled in Syria and died there. What Shaddad narrated: Usama ibn Umayr al-Hudhali from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him. Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Wasil ibn Abd al-Ala from Muhammad ibn Fudayl from Hajjaj from Abu Malih from his father from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Circumcision is a sunna for men and an honor for women."
"7139","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Massisi from Arim Abu al-Numan from Hafs ibn Ghiyath from Hajjaj ibn Artah from Abu al-Malih from his father from Shaddad ibn Aws, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Circumcision is a sunna for men and an honor for women."
"7140","Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Shaddad. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari - Abd al-Razzaq informed us - from al-Razi from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I memorized two things from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Allah, Almighty and Exalted, has prescribed excellence upon everything; so when you kill, kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well, and let one of you sharpen his blade, then let him rest his slaughtered animal."
"7141","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Shuba from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: Two traits I heard them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah has prescribed excellence upon everything; so when you kill, kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well, and let one of you sharpen his blade, and let him rest his slaughtered animal."
"7142","Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from Sahl ibn Bakkar from Wahb from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, Almighty and Exalted, has prescribed excellence upon everything; so when you kill, kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well, and let one of you sharpen his blade, and let him rest his slaughtered animal."
"7143","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman from Abu Hafs al-Abbar from al-Amash from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Almighty and Exalted, has prescribed excellence upon everything; so when you kill, kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well, and let one of you sharpen his blade, and let him rest his slaughtered animal."
"7144","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Jarir from Mansur from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has prescribed excellence upon everything; so when you kill, kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well, and let one of you sharpen his blade, and let him rest his slaughtered animal."
"7145","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Hushaym and Khalid ibn Abd Allah from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I memorized two traits from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah has prescribed excellence upon everything... and he mentioned similar to it."
"7146","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Ismail from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: Two things I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah, Almighty and Exalted, has prescribed excellence upon everything... and he mentioned similar to it."
"7147","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari - Abd al-Razzaq informed us - from Mamar from Ayyub from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I memorized two things from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Allah, Almighty and Exalted, is Excellent and loves excellence; so when you kill, kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well, and let one of you sharpen his blade, then let him rest his slaughtered animal."
"7148","Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from Sahl ibn Bakkar from Wahb from Ayyub from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, Almighty and Exalted, has prescribed excellence upon everything; so when you kill, kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well, and let one of you sharpen his blade, and let him rest his slaughtered animal."
"7149","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani from Ismail ibn Abi al-Harith from Shababa ibn Sawwar from Shuba from Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Almighty and Exalted, has prescribed excellence upon everything; so when you kill, kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well, and let one of you sharpen his blade, and let him rest his slaughtered animal."
"7150","Chapter. Narrated Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi from Abu Hudhayfa from Sufyan from Khalid al-Hadhdha and Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7151","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari - Abd al-Razzaq informed us - from Mamar from Asim ibn Sulayman from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man being cupped on the eighteenth of Ramadan, while I was with him, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7152","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from al-Husayn ibn Salama ibn Abi Kabsha from Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani, and narrated Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai from Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar from Abd al-Ala, both saying: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us from Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7153","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal - my father narrated to me - from Ismail ibn Ibrahim from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Shaddad ibn Aws, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a man being cupped at al-Baqi on the eighteenth night past of Ramadan, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7154","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad, and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, both saying: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man being cupped at the time of the Conquest, on the eighteenth night past of Ramadan, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7155","Narrated Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani from Abu Umayya Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Khallad al-Wasiti from Amr ibn Awn - Hushaym informed us - from Mansur ibn Zadham and Khalid, from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Conquest, and he passed by a man being cupped on the eighteenth or seventeenth in Ramadan, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7156","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani from Said ibn Abi Hani from his father from Sufyan from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Maqil ibn Yasar in the month of Ramadan while he was being cupped, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7157","Narrated Musa ibn Ishaq, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad, saying: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us from Suwayd Abu Hatim from Qatada from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man being cupped in Ramadan, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7158","Narrated Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati from Abu Nuaym from Abu Qahdham, and narrated Muhammad ibn Yaqub al-Khatib from Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid from Abu Qahdham from Abu Qilaba - Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani narrated to us - that Shaddad ibn Aws narrated to him, saying: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of the roads of al-Madina, while he was holding my hand, when he saw a man being cupped in Ramadan, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7159","Chapter. Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Qazaa ibn Suwayd from Abu Asim from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever composes a verse of poetry after Isha, Allah will not accept his prayer that night."
"7160","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi from Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak from Ismail ibn Ayyash from Rashid ibn Dawud from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever washes and bathes on Friday, and goes early and arrives early, then sits close to the imam, listens and is silent, will have for every step he takes the deed of a year - its fasting and its standing in prayer."
"7161","Narrated Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi and Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Hadhdham al-Dimashqi, both saying: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Ismail ibn Ayyash - Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Rahabi narrated to me - from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Shaddad ibn Aws, when you see people hoarding gold and silver, then hoard these words: O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in the matter, and resolve upon guidance, and I ask You for what makes Your mercy obligatory, and firm resolves of Your forgiveness, and I ask You for gratitude for Your blessing, and excellence of Your worship, and I ask You for a sound heart, and a truthful tongue, and I ask You of the best of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know; indeed You are the Knower of the unseen."
"7162","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi from Hisham ibn Ammar, and narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti from his father, and narrated Musa ibn Harun from al-Haytham ibn Kharija, all saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Rashid ibn Dawud al-Sanani from Abu al-Ashath, that he went early to the mosque of Damascus, hastening in going; and he met Shaddad ibn Aws al-Ansari, with al-Sunabihi with him; I said: Where are you going, may Allah have mercy on you both? They said: We intend here to visit a sick brother of ours; so I set out with them until they entered upon him; and they said to him: How have you woken? He said: I have woken in blessing and favor; so Shaddad said to him: Rejoice in expiations of evil deeds and removal of sins; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Almighty and Exalted, says: When I afflict a believing servant of Mine, and he praises Me for what I afflicted him with, then he rises from his bed as on the day his mother bore him, free of sins; and the Lord, Almighty and Exalted, says: I have confined this servant of Mine, and afflicted him, so record for him what you used to record for him before that while he was healthy."
"7163","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Ismail ibn Abi al-Harith from Shababa ibn Sawwar from Kharija ibn Musab from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the strap of one of your sandals breaks, let him not walk in a single sandal."
"7164","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm al-Ashari from Shaddad ibn Aws. Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih from Abd Allah ibn Salih - Ibn Lahia narrated to me - from Ibn Anum from Ubada ibn Nusayy from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm - Muadh ibn Jabal, Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah, Ubada ibn al-Samit and Shaddad ibn Aws narrated to us - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman, if she kills deliberately, is not executed until she delivers what is in her womb if she is pregnant, and until she entrusts her child to a guardian; and if she commits adultery, she is not stoned until she delivers what is in her womb, and until she entrusts her child to a guardian."
"7165","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratis from Asad ibn Musa, and narrated Abu Khalifa from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, and narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Asim ibn Ali, all saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays to show off has committed shirk, and whoever fasts to show off has committed shirk, and whoever gives charity to show off has committed shirk."
"7166","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratis from Asad ibn Musa, and narrated Abu Khalifa from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, and narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abd Allah ibn Raja, all saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from Shaddad ibn Aws, who narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst of this nation will surely follow the ways of those before them among the People of the Book, exactly alike."
"7167","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Salam al-Bayruti Mak-hul from Ibrahim ibn Amr ibn Bakr al-Saksaki, who said: I heard my father narrating from Thawr ibn Yazid and Ghalib ibn Abd Allah from Makhul from Ibn Ghanm from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The intelligent one is he who subdues his soul and works for what is after death, and the incapable one is he who makes his soul follow its desire and wishes upon Allah."
"7168","Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Shaddad ibn Aws. Narrated Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi from his father, and narrated Umara ibn Wathima al-Misri from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq from Amr ibn al-Harith from Abd Allah ibn Salim from al-Zubaydi - al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us - that Jubayr ibn Nufayr said: Shaddad ibn Aws narrated to us, saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how were you taken by night on the night you were taken? He said: I prayed Isha with my companions at Makka in the dark, then Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me with a white mount, above a donkey and below a mule, and said: Ride; and it proved refractory to me, so he turned it by its ear, then mounted me upon it; and it set out gliding with us, its hoof falling where its glance reached, until we reached a land of date-palms; and he said: Dismount; so I dismounted; then he said: Pray; so I prayed; then we rode, and he said: Do you know where you prayed? I said: Allah knows best. He said: You prayed at Yathrib, you prayed at Tayba. Then it set out gliding with us, its hoof falling where its glance reached, until we reached a white land; and he said: Dismount; so I dismounted; then he said: Pray; so I prayed; then we rode, and he said: Do you know where you prayed? I said: Allah knows best. He said: You prayed at Madyan, you prayed at the tree of Musa. Then it set out gliding with us, its hoof falling where its glance reached, then we reached a land whose palaces appeared to us; and he said: Dismount; so I dismounted; then he said: Pray; so I prayed; and he said: Do you know where you prayed? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: You prayed at Bayt Lahm where Isa, peace be upon him, the Messiah son of Maryam, was born. Then he took me until we entered the city from its Yemeni gate, and came to the qibla of the mosque, tied his mount, and we entered the mosque from a gate where the sun inclines; and I prayed in the mosque where Allah willed; and I was seized by thirst most severely, and I was brought two vessels, in one milk and in the other honey, sent to me together; and I weighed between them, then Allah guided me, and I took the milk and drank until it rang against my forehead; and before me was an old man reclining on his cushion, and he said: Your companion has taken the fitra; he will indeed be guided. Then he took me until we came to the valley in the city, and Hell was uncovered like carpets; and we said: O Messenger of Allah, how did you find it? He said: Like intensely hot fever. Then he turned back with me, and we passed by a caravan of Quraysh at such-and-such place; they had lost a camel of theirs which so-and-so had gathered for them; and I greeted them, and one of them said: This is the voice of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then I came to my companions before dawn at Makka; and Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, came to me and said: O Messenger of Allah, where were you tonight, for I sought you in your place? He said: Did you know that I came to the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis tonight? He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a month's journey; so describe it to me; and its sight was opened to me, as if I were looking at it; they did not ask me about anything but I informed them of it; and Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. And the polytheists said: Look at the son of Abu Kabsha claiming he came to Bayt al-Maqdis tonight. He said: Among the signs of what I tell you is that I passed by a caravan of yours at such-and-such place, led by a dusky camel upon it a black hair-cloth and two black sacks. Then when that day came, the people looked out until near midday, until the people came led by that camel which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had described."
"7169","Damra ibn Habib from Shaddad ibn Aws. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki, both saying: Said ibn Mansur narrated to us from Ibn al-Mubarak from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam from Damra ibn Habib from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The intelligent one is he who subdues his soul and works for what is after death, and the incapable one is he who makes his soul follow its desire and wishes upon Allah."
"7170","Ubada ibn Nusayy from Shaddad. Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from Yazid ibn Mawhab al-Ramli from Ibn Wahb - al-Harith ibn Nabhan narrated to me - from Abd al-Wahid ibn Zayd from Ubada ibn Nusayy, who said: I entered upon Shaddad ibn Aws while he was weeping, and he said: Two hadiths I heard them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I said: And what are they? He said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw in his face something that grieved me; I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this I see in your face? He said: Two matters I fear for my nation after me: shirk, and hidden desire; indeed they will not worship sun, nor moon, nor stone, nor idol, but they will show off with their deeds. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, is that shirk? He said: Yes. I said: And what is hidden desire? He said: A servant wakes fasting, then a desire of his desires presents itself to him, so he commits it and abandons his fast."
"7171","Narrated Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Yazid al-Sulami al-Basri from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Abd al-Wahid ibn Zayd from Ubada ibn Nusayy, who said: I entered upon Shaddad ibn Aws while he was weeping, and I said: What makes you weep, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: For a hadith I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mentioning it: Among the most fearful of what I fear for my nation: shirk with Allah, and hidden desire; a man wakes fasting, then sees something he desires, so he commits it; and shirk is a people who do not worship stone nor idol, but they do a deed to show off."
"7172","Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Shaddad. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Hudba ibn Khalid from Hammad ibn Salama from Ashath ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jarmi from Abu Qilaba from Abu Asma from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Almighty and Exalted, wrote a Book before He created the heavens and the earth by two thousand years, and sent down in it two verses with which He sealed Surat al-Baqara; they are not recited in a house three nights, then a devil approaches it."
"7173","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from Ayyub from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Abu Asma from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7174","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab from Hammad ibn Zayd from Ayyub from Abu Qilaba - I know it only from Abu al-Ashath - from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of the roads of al-Madina, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was holding my hand, on the eighteenth night past of Ramadan, when he came upon a man being cupped, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7175","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Bashshar from Sahl ibn Yusuf from al-Muthanna ibn Sad Abu Affan from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath from Abu Asma from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was holding my hand, on the eighteenth night past of Ramadan, when he turned and saw a man being cupped, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7176","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani, and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, and narrated Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai from Ali ibn al-Mundhir, all saying: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from Abd Allah ibn Zayd from Abu al-Ashath from Abu Asma from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed on the eighteenth night past of Ramadan, and saw a man being cupped, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7177","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal from Hammad from Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a man being cupped on the eighteenth night past of Ramadan, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7178","Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami and Qays ibn Jafar al-Darimi, both saying: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us from Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Qilaba from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was holding my hand, on the morning of the eighteenth; and he glanced, and saw a man being cupped, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7179","Narrated Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi from Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Attar from Amr ibn Asim from Hammam from Qatada from Abu Qilaba from Abu Asma from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the eighteenth past of Ramadan, and he saw a man being cupped, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7180","Narrated Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani from Ahmad ibn Sinan from Yazid ibn Harun from Ayyub Abu al-Ala from Qatada from Abu Asma from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the eighteenth of Ramadan, and he saw a man being cupped, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"7181","Narrated Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi from his grandfather Ibrahim ibn al-Ala from Ismail ibn Ayyash from Rashid ibn Dawud al-Sanani from Abu Asma al-Rahabi from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There will be over you leaders who kill prayer from its times; so pray prayer at its time, and make your prayer with them supererogatory."
"7182","Abu Idris al-Khawlani from Shaddad ibn Aws. Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Abd al-Mumin ibn Ali - Abd al-Salam ibn Harb informed us - from Burd ibn Sinan from Makhul from Abu Idris - more than one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me, among them Shaddad ibn Aws and Thawban - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pen is lifted in hadd from the child until he grows up, and from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the insane until he recovers, and from the afflicted imbecile."
"7183","Abu Ubayd Allah Muslim ibn Mishkam from Shaddad. Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Abi Zura al-Dimashqi, both saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us from Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Awzai from Hassan ibn Atiyya from Abu Ubayd Allah Muslim ibn Mishkam, that he heard Shaddad ibn Aws saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When people hoard dinars and dirhams, then hoard these words: O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in the matter, and resolve upon guidance, and I ask You for gratitude for Your blessing, and excellence of Your worship, and I ask You of the best of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know."
"7184","Kathir ibn Murra al-Hadrami from Shaddad. Narrated Abu Yazid al-Hawti from Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi from Abu Mahdi Said ibn Sinan from Abu al-Zahiriyya from Abu Shajara Kathir ibn Murra from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O people, this world is a present commodity from which the righteous and the wicked eat, and the Hereafter is a true promise, in which a Capable King judges, establishing truth by it and nullifying falsehood; O people, be children of the Hereafter, and do not be children of this world, for every mother is followed by her child."
"7185","Abu al-Musabbih al-Maqrai from Shaddad ibn Aws. Narrated Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sufyan al-Raqqi from Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan from Marwan ibn Muawiya al-Fazari from Muhammad ibn Abi Qays al-Shami from Abu Musabbih al-Himsi, who said: I sat with a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them Shaddad ibn Aws and Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while they were discussing; and they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may do such-and-such good, yet he is a hypocrite. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how can he be a hypocrite while he believes in you? He said: He curses the leaders and reviles them."
"7186","Yala ibn Shaddad ibn Aws from his father. Narrated Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughba from Said ibn Abi Maryam - Ibn Lahia informed us - from Umara ibn Ghaziyya from Yala ibn Shaddad ibn Aws from his father, who said: We used to count showing off in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as minor shirk."
"7187","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih from Said ibn Ufayr - Shaddad ibn Abd al-Rahman, of the descendants of Shaddad ibn Aws, narrated to me - from his father from Yala ibn Shaddad from his father, that he entered upon Muawiya, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was sitting with Amr ibn al-As on his bed; and Shaddad sat between them and said: Do you know what seats me between you? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you see them together, separate between them; for by Allah they have not gathered except upon treachery. So I wished to separate between you."
"7188","Narrated Ali ibn Said al-Razi from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Wara from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Shaddad ibn Muhammad ibn Shaddad, who said: I heard my father mentioning, from his father, from his grandfather, from Shaddad ibn Aws, that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was breathing his last; and he said: What is wrong with you, O Shaddad? He said: The world has grown strait for me. He said: It is not upon you; Syria will be conquered, and Bayt al-Maqdis will be conquered, and you and your child will be leaders among them, if Allah wills."
"7189","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, both saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Sanani from Rashid ibn Dawud al-Sanani - Yala ibn Shaddad ibn Aws narrated to us - from his father, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house of a man of his Companions, and he said: Look, is there any stranger among you? They said: No. He said: Lock the door. So the door was locked. Then he said: Raise your hands and say: There is no god but Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised, and we raised our hands. Then he said: Lower your hands and rejoice, for you have been forgiven; I was sent with it, and with it I was commanded, and upon it I shall enter Paradise."
"7190","Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from Abu Muawiya from Hilal ibn Maymun from Yala ibn Shaddad from his father, or another of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Hilal doubted - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray in your sandals, and do not resemble the Jews."
"7191","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi from Hisham ibn Ammar from Marwan ibn Muawiya from Hilal ibn Maymun from Yala ibn Shaddad ibn Aws from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray in your sandals; oppose the Jews."
"7192","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Harmala ibn Yahya from Ibn Wahb - Ibn Lahia informed me - from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughira from Yala ibn Shaddad ibn Aws from his father, who said: Abu Dharr would hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a command containing strictness, then go out to his desert; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would later grant a concession in it, and the concession from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in that matter would be preserved, but Abu Dharr would not hear it; so Abu Dharr would hold to the first command he had heard before that."
"7193","Mahmud ibn al-Rabi from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani from Abu Masud Ahmad ibn al-Furat from Sahl ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Sindi from Amr ibn Abi Qays from Ghaylan ibn Jami from Humayd al-Shami from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah gathers the first and the last in a single expanse, sight piercing through them and the caller making them hear, He says: I am the best partner; every deed done for Me in the abode of this world in which there was a partner for Me, I abandon it today, and I accept today only what is sincere. Then he recited: Except the sincere servants of Allah; and: So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord, let him do righteous deed and not associate in the worship of his Lord anyone."
"7194","Mahmud ibn Labid from Shaddad ibn Aws. Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin al-Muqri and Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami, both saying: Qazaa ibn Suwayd narrated to us from Humayd al-Araj from al-Zuhri from Mahmud ibn Labid from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you attend your dead, close the eyes, for sight follows the soul, and say good, for it is said amen to what the household says."
"7195","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal - Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to me - and narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki from Hafs ibn Umar al-Juddi from Qazaa ibn Suwayd from Yahya ibn Jurja from al-Zuhri from Mahmud ibn Labid from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: He is not a liar who speaks good or conveys good."
"7196","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami from Qazaa ibn Suwayd from Yahya ibn Jurja from al-Zuhri from Mahmud ibn Labid from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land will be collared with it from seven earths; and whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"7197","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Suwayd ibn Said from al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari from al-Zuhri from Mahmud ibn Labid from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To leave your heirs rich is better than to leave them dependent begging people; and you will not spend any spending seeking thereby the Face of Allah but you will be rewarded for it, even what you place in your wife's mouth."
"7198","Bushayr ibn Kab al-Adawi from Shaddad. Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi from Murajja ibn Raja from Husayn al-Muallim from Abd Allah ibn Burayda from Bushayr ibn Kab al-Adawi from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The master of seeking forgiveness is that you say: O Allah, You are my Lord; there is no god but You; You created me and I am Your servant, and upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I can; I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done, and I acknowledge Your blessing upon me, and I acknowledge my sin; so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You. If he says it after evening comes, then dies that night, he enters Paradise; and if he says it after morning comes, then dies that day, he enters Paradise."
"7199","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yazid ibn Zuray from Husayn al-Muallim from Abd Allah ibn Burayda from Bushayr ibn Kab from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"7200","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Abu Usama from Husayn al-Muallim from Abd Allah ibn Burayda from Bushayr ibn Kab from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
